-[PANTING]
-[DISTANT SHOUTING]

62
00:07:22,210 --> 00:07:24,179
-[WIND HOWLING]
-[LOW GROWLING]

63
00:07:33,355 --> 00:07:35,324
[PANTING]

64
00:07:39,661 --> 00:07:42,230
[WOLVES HOWLING]

65
00:07:45,567 --> 00:07:47,536
-[PANTING]
-[WOLF SNARLING]

66
00:07:49,571 --> 00:07:51,707
[BARKING, SNARLING]

67
00:07:54,343 --> 00:07:56,345
[WHINES SOFTLY]

68
00:07:58,947 --> 00:07:59,881
[WHINES]

69
00:08:00,015 --> 00:08:01,950
[PANTING]

70
00:08:02,951 --> 00:08:04,586
[GRUNTING]

71
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,822
Move! Move! Move!

72
00:08:26,808 --> 00:08:28,810
PILOT: [OVER RADIO]
<i>You were late.</i>

73
00:08:28,944 --> 00:08:31,780
<i>Next time, you break out of</i>
<i>prison and I fly this thing.</i>

74
00:08:31,913 --> 00:08:33,882
No, thanks.

75
00:08:34,016 --> 00:08:35,217
<i>So, how'd it go?</i>

76
00:08:35,350 --> 00:08:37,953
How it always goes.

77
00:08:38,086 --> 00:08:40,222
Good for me...

78
00:08:40,355 --> 00:08:42,024
bad for him.

79
00:08:45,961 --> 00:08:47,195
[HEADPHONES DROP TO FLOOR]

80
00:09:05,647 --> 00:09:07,115
SOLDIER:
<i>Nyet.</i>

81
00:09:21,229 --> 00:09:22,230
[ROARING]

82
00:09:26,368 --> 00:09:28,370
[LOW SNARLING]

83
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:40,682
[SEAGULLS SCREECHING]

84
00:09:45,053 --> 00:09:47,055
[STUDENTS SPEAKING
INDISTINCTLY, LAUGHING]

85
00:09:50,692 --> 00:09:52,727
[WHISTLE BLOWING]

86
00:09:52,861 --> 00:09:54,596
Kravinoff and Kravinoff!

87
00:09:54,729 --> 00:09:57,099
Your father is coming
to pick you up!

88
00:10:03,872 --> 00:10:05,774
What'd you do?

89
00:10:05,907 --> 00:10:07,275
Me?

90
00:10:07,409 --> 00:10:08,910
[CHUCKLES]
Nothing. I thought it was you.

91
00:10:09,044 --> 00:10:10,011
No.

92
00:10:14,449 --> 00:10:16,451
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

93
00:10:29,264 --> 00:10:31,199
[SIGHS]

94
00:10:32,267 --> 00:10:34,302
Where are we going, Papa?

95
00:10:34,436 --> 00:10:36,271
We're in the middle of a term
at school.

96
00:10:36,404 --> 00:10:37,672
Sergei...

97
00:10:37,806 --> 00:10:39,274
Mom never made us
do shit like this.

98
00:10:39,407 --> 00:10:41,009
Sergei...

99
00:10:42,578 --> 00:10:44,412
...your mother is dead.

100
00:10:45,447 --> 00:10:47,015
She took own life.

101
00:10:47,149 --> 00:10:49,351
She was weak.

102
00:10:49,484 --> 00:10:51,621
Sick in her mind.

103
00:10:53,388 --> 00:10:55,390
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

104
00:10:55,525 --> 00:10:58,693
It was her choice.

105
00:10:58,827 --> 00:11:00,695
Well, she died
because you sent her away.

106
00:11:00,829 --> 00:11:02,632
No.

107
00:11:02,764 --> 00:11:04,966
She gave up long ago.

108
00:11:06,134 --> 00:11:08,770
You haven't even seen her
for two years.

109
00:11:09,838 --> 00:11:11,907
Nothing will change for you.

110
00:11:12,040 --> 00:11:13,808
Or for you, Dmitri.

111
00:11:13,942 --> 00:11:17,012
Where are we going, Papa?
To the funeral?

112
00:11:17,145 --> 00:11:20,015
If you take own life, you do
not get honor of funeral.

113
00:11:20,148 --> 00:11:22,184
So then, where are
you taking us?

114
00:11:22,317 --> 00:11:23,985
We go to hunt.

115
00:11:24,119 --> 00:11:27,989
There have been new sightings
of lion, Zar.

116
00:11:28,123 --> 00:11:29,858
It will be good for you.

117
00:11:29,991 --> 00:11:31,026
Both.

118
00:11:32,127 --> 00:11:34,829
To join men,
be one with nature.

119
00:11:35,864 --> 00:11:37,866
Shoot to kill.

120
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,202
Fun.

121
00:11:42,070 --> 00:11:44,072
[JET ENGINE WHIRRING]

122
00:11:57,219 --> 00:11:59,988
GRANDMOTHER:
Careful with those.

123
00:12:00,121 --> 00:12:02,724
Put the cards away now,
Calypso.

124
00:12:02,857 --> 00:12:04,793
Your mum and dad
will be back soon,

125
00:12:04,926 --> 00:12:07,530
and you know the way
they feel about all this.

126
00:12:07,663 --> 00:12:09,998
It's just a game, Granny.

127
00:12:10,131 --> 00:12:13,235
You think my cards
are just pretty pictures.

128
00:12:14,236 --> 00:12:16,905
Think again, Calypso.

129
00:12:17,038 --> 00:12:20,742
They show us the unseen road.

130
00:12:20,875 --> 00:12:22,077
What?

131
00:12:22,210 --> 00:12:24,779
-Like, predict the future?
-Mm-hmm.

132
00:12:24,913 --> 00:12:26,948
In the right hands.

133
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:34,523
Lay three cards down.

134
00:12:35,725 --> 00:12:38,393
The first card is the subject.

135
00:12:38,527 --> 00:12:41,129
CALYPSO:
The High Priestess?

136
00:12:41,263 --> 00:12:44,600
You do come from a long line
of very powerful women.

137
00:12:44,734 --> 00:12:47,703
The second card is
the situation.

138
00:12:48,870 --> 00:12:50,405
The Tower.

139
00:12:50,539 --> 00:12:53,743
There's going to be
a terrible accident.

140
00:12:55,443 --> 00:12:58,346
The third card is the outcome.

141
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,750
Strength.

142
00:13:00,882 --> 00:13:03,952
There is great danger
in that card.

143
00:13:04,085 --> 00:13:06,488
I have something
for you, Calypso.

144
00:13:06,622 --> 00:13:09,157
I was going to wait
until you were older,

145
00:13:09,291 --> 00:13:12,794
but the cards have shown us
you will need it very soon.

146
00:13:12,927 --> 00:13:14,195
What is it?

147
00:13:14,329 --> 00:13:15,864
A potion.

148
00:13:15,997 --> 00:13:18,300
The formula has been
passed down

149
00:13:18,433 --> 00:13:21,269
in our family for generations.

150
00:13:22,337 --> 00:13:24,272
What does that symbol mean?

151
00:13:24,406 --> 00:13:28,310
GRANDMOTHER: It's a sign
of the spirit Papa Legba.

152
00:13:28,443 --> 00:13:31,446
He opens the gate
to the other side.

153
00:13:31,580 --> 00:13:32,981
Protect it.

154
00:13:33,114 --> 00:13:35,751
Very powerful.

155
00:13:37,085 --> 00:13:38,721
Go ahead.

156
00:13:38,853 --> 00:13:43,925
It will heal whoever drinks it
in undreamed-of ways.

157
00:13:44,059 --> 00:13:46,796
The time is coming soon.

158
00:13:46,928 --> 00:13:49,831
You'll know what to do with it.

159
00:13:49,964 --> 00:13:53,835
Now, put those away
before your parents get back.

160
00:14:03,011 --> 00:14:05,781
[BIRDS CAWING]

161
00:14:05,914 --> 00:14:07,882
[GUNSHOT ECHOES]

162
00:14:10,786 --> 00:14:12,688
Well done, Nikolai.

163
00:14:19,528 --> 00:14:21,996
[ANTELOPE WHEEZING QUIETLY]

164
00:14:22,130 --> 00:14:23,532
Sergei.

165
00:14:30,305 --> 00:14:33,843
You see? So beautiful.

166
00:14:36,277 --> 00:14:37,813
Never fear death.

167
00:14:38,880 --> 00:14:40,716
They are prey.

168
00:14:40,850 --> 00:14:43,418
We are predators.

169
00:14:49,357 --> 00:14:55,029
Men should be only animal
that is dreaded.

170
00:14:59,802 --> 00:15:03,238
Dmitri, don't look so weak.

171
00:15:04,507 --> 00:15:06,374
Be a man.

172
00:15:09,077 --> 00:15:10,345
[INSECTS CHIRPING]

173
00:15:10,478 --> 00:15:11,714
SERGEI:
You all right?

174
00:15:11,847 --> 00:15:13,114
DMITRI:
Yeah.

175
00:15:14,717 --> 00:15:16,719
He shouldn't have talked
to you like that.

176
00:15:16,852 --> 00:15:18,821
Yeah, well...

177
00:15:20,255 --> 00:15:22,123
...he's an asshole.

178
00:15:22,257 --> 00:15:24,259
There's nothing
I can do about that.

179
00:15:24,392 --> 00:15:27,830
He'll never respect me
like he respects you.

180
00:15:27,962 --> 00:15:29,130
Want to bet?

181
00:15:33,201 --> 00:15:34,603
[LAUGHS SOFTLY]

182
00:15:37,305 --> 00:15:39,073
[SERGEI SIGHS]

183
00:15:39,207 --> 00:15:41,610
DMITRI:
I miss Mom.

184
00:15:41,744 --> 00:15:44,479
SERGEI:
Me, too, Dima. Me, too.

185
00:15:46,281 --> 00:15:48,983
[LION ROARING IN DISTANCE]

186
00:15:51,119 --> 00:15:53,121
Is it the Zar?

187
00:15:53,254 --> 00:15:54,790
Not even pussycat.

188
00:15:54,924 --> 00:15:56,892
Perhaps it's the Zar's
illegitimate half-brother.

189
00:15:57,025 --> 00:15:58,259
[CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

190
00:15:58,393 --> 00:15:59,494
Like your Dmitri.

191
00:15:59,628 --> 00:16:01,396
NIKOLAI:
Leave the boy.

192
00:16:01,530 --> 00:16:05,200
He carries no blame
for his father's wandering eye.

193
00:16:05,333 --> 00:16:08,102
You will know Zar
when you hear.

194
00:16:08,236 --> 00:16:12,340
He sound like thunder
from mountaintop.

195
00:16:12,474 --> 00:16:14,510
You have seen this beast?

196
00:16:14,643 --> 00:16:18,146
I have seen his work.

197
00:16:18,279 --> 00:16:22,685
This cat has killed two dozen,
maybe three dozen men.

198
00:16:22,818 --> 00:16:24,920
Yes?

199
00:16:25,086 --> 00:16:27,523
For as long as men like you
have been coming down here

200
00:16:27,656 --> 00:16:29,190
to kill lions,

201
00:16:29,324 --> 00:16:32,962
there have been legends
of the one who can't be killed.

202
00:16:33,094 --> 00:16:35,430
NIKOLAI:
Men like me.

203
00:16:35,564 --> 00:16:38,701
But you still take my money,
don't you, Bahari?

204
00:16:39,768 --> 00:16:41,837
A lion hunts for food.

205
00:16:43,071 --> 00:16:44,640
Same as I do.

206
00:16:49,477 --> 00:16:52,013
Why do you hunt, Nikolai?

207
00:16:52,146 --> 00:16:53,682
You know this, Bahari.

208
00:16:55,316 --> 00:16:59,354
Men who kill legend
becomes legend.

209
00:17:00,856 --> 00:17:03,659
[DISTANT THUNDER RUMBLING]

210
00:17:03,792 --> 00:17:05,794
ALEKSEI: [BREATHLESSLY]
Nikolai...

211
00:17:05,928 --> 00:17:07,228
we should talk.

212
00:17:07,362 --> 00:17:09,163
Save your breath.

213
00:17:09,297 --> 00:17:11,000
No, it's a condition.

214
00:17:11,132 --> 00:17:15,203
I'll be okay, as long as I take
a few breaks here and there.

215
00:17:15,336 --> 00:17:17,506
One thing that you should know
about me is that

216
00:17:17,640 --> 00:17:19,340
I'm always thinking
of the future.

217
00:17:20,776 --> 00:17:23,044
I want you to be my partner.

218
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,447
What is your name?

219
00:17:28,717 --> 00:17:31,754
I'm a guest here of Vladimir.

220
00:17:32,821 --> 00:17:34,523
Aleksei Sytsevich.

221
00:17:34,657 --> 00:17:36,725
No.

222
00:17:36,859 --> 00:17:38,761
You do not have name.

223
00:17:40,996 --> 00:17:44,232
In this world,
you barely exist.

224
00:17:44,365 --> 00:17:46,835
So, what can some
no-name, nonexistent,

225
00:17:46,969 --> 00:17:50,539
condition-suffering fool
offer up to the Kravinoffs?

226
00:17:51,574 --> 00:17:53,542
-Nothing.
-[SHORT CHUCKLE]

227
00:17:53,676 --> 00:17:56,545
I am here...

228
00:17:56,679 --> 00:18:00,214
teaching my sons
the joy of stalking,

229
00:18:00,348 --> 00:18:04,954
and you and your imbecilic
voice are stalking me.

230
00:18:06,522 --> 00:18:07,790
So, be quiet.

231
00:18:17,131 --> 00:18:19,802
Hope Father gets him this time.

232
00:18:19,935 --> 00:18:21,302
Why?

233
00:18:21,436 --> 00:18:22,905
Well, because then
he'll become a legend,

234
00:18:23,038 --> 00:18:24,907
and we don't have
to come here again.

235
00:18:28,142 --> 00:18:30,178
A true legend would fight fair.

236
00:18:30,311 --> 00:18:32,280
Not with a gun.

237
00:18:32,413 --> 00:18:34,550
You would do it one-on-one
with only the tools

238
00:18:34,683 --> 00:18:35,784
you were born with.

239
00:18:35,918 --> 00:18:37,553
[LOW GROWLING NEARBY]

240
00:18:44,059 --> 00:18:45,628
Dmitri...

241
00:18:45,761 --> 00:18:47,763
get back.

242
00:18:58,306 --> 00:19:00,009
[LOW GROWLING]

243
00:19:00,141 --> 00:19:02,143
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

244
00:19:06,749 --> 00:19:08,784
[LOW SNARLING]

245
00:19:16,659 --> 00:19:18,159
[SNARLING STOPS]

246
00:19:18,292 --> 00:19:20,763
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

247
00:19:20,896 --> 00:19:22,998
-[GUNSHOT]
-[SERGEI GASPS]

248
00:19:23,132 --> 00:19:24,332
-[ROARING]
-Dmitri, move!

249
00:19:24,465 --> 00:19:25,834
Move!

250
00:19:26,902 --> 00:19:28,704
[SERGEI CRIES OUT]

251
00:19:29,505 --> 00:19:31,006
Run!

252
00:19:31,140 --> 00:19:33,042
-[GUNSHOT]
-[ROARS]

253
00:19:33,174 --> 00:19:35,144
SERGEI:
Run! [SCREAMING]

254
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:39,715
[WHIMPERING, SCREAMING]

255
00:19:39,848 --> 00:19:41,984
[SCREAM ECHOING]

256
00:19:42,117 --> 00:19:43,886
[ROARS]

257
00:19:44,953 --> 00:19:47,255
NIKOLAI: [ECHOING]
Sergei!

258
00:19:47,388 --> 00:19:48,724
[LOW GROWLING]

259
00:19:48,857 --> 00:19:51,660
Sergei!

260
00:20:06,542 --> 00:20:08,177
[LAUGHS]
Oh.

261
00:20:08,309 --> 00:20:10,311
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

262
00:20:11,345 --> 00:20:13,381
Calypso, look.

263
00:20:19,822 --> 00:20:21,790
[CAMERA SHUTTER CLICKING]

264
00:20:25,160 --> 00:20:27,196
[DISTANT THUNDER RUMBLING]

265
00:20:28,664 --> 00:20:30,733
CALYPSO'S MUM:
Come on, honey, stand up.

266
00:20:30,866 --> 00:20:32,868
[BIRDS CAWING]

267
00:20:34,002 --> 00:20:35,403
Calypso?

268
00:20:36,672 --> 00:20:38,372
Calypso?

269
00:20:38,507 --> 00:20:39,608
[SIGHS]

270
00:20:41,375 --> 00:20:43,244
Calypso!

271
00:20:43,377 --> 00:20:45,379
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

272
00:20:46,515 --> 00:20:48,617
[LOW GROWLING NEARBY]

273
00:20:53,856 --> 00:20:55,691
[GROWLING]

274
00:21:01,897 --> 00:21:04,265
[EERIE VOICES ECHOING]

275
00:21:08,737 --> 00:21:10,639
[GROWLS]

276
00:21:35,264 --> 00:21:37,132
[ROARING, SNARLING]

277
00:21:37,266 --> 00:21:39,601
GRANDMOTHER:
<i>In the name of all the spirits</i>

278
00:21:39,735 --> 00:21:41,402
<i>and all the mysteries...</i>

279
00:21:41,537 --> 00:21:42,805
[ECHOING]
<i>mysteries...</i>

280
00:21:46,575 --> 00:21:48,143
CALYPSO: [ECHOING]
Help!

281
00:21:48,277 --> 00:21:49,878
[LOW GROWLING]

282
00:21:51,914 --> 00:21:55,150
GRANDMOTHER: [ECHOING]
<i>Bring the power of the earth.</i>

283
00:21:55,284 --> 00:21:57,820
[ECHOING]
<i>...the power of the earth.</i>

284
00:21:57,953 --> 00:21:59,453
[HELICOPTER BLADES WHIRRING]

285
00:22:06,695 --> 00:22:08,462
Wait.

286
00:22:16,505 --> 00:22:18,140
[RINGING TONE]

287
00:22:18,273 --> 00:22:19,808
-[BIRD SCREECHING]
-GRANDMOTHER: <i>Bring the power</i>

288
00:22:19,942 --> 00:22:21,677
[ECHOING]
<i>of the sky.</i>

289
00:22:21,810 --> 00:22:23,812
[WIND WHISTLING]

290
00:22:25,314 --> 00:22:27,282
[FLATLINE TONE BEEPING]

291
00:22:28,650 --> 00:22:30,619
Everybody's clear.
Shocking now.

292
00:22:30,752 --> 00:22:32,120
[ELECTRICAL THUMP]

293
00:22:33,155 --> 00:22:36,490
[FLATLINE TONE CONTINUES]

294
00:22:36,625 --> 00:22:38,861
Okay, team,
we've done all we can.

295
00:22:38,994 --> 00:22:42,831
I'm going to call
time of death, 6:51.

296
00:22:42,965 --> 00:22:44,900
[FLATLINE TONE CONTINUES]

297
00:22:50,973 --> 00:22:52,841
[SNARLING]

298
00:22:58,614 --> 00:23:00,148
-[ROARS]
-[GASPS]

299
00:23:00,282 --> 00:23:02,251
-[MONITOR BEEPING STEADILY]
-[BREATHING SOFTLY]

300
00:23:10,491 --> 00:23:12,460
[INDISTINCT P.A. ANNOUNCEMENT]

301
00:23:15,731 --> 00:23:19,001
DOCTOR: The EMTs found
that card in your pocket.

302
00:23:19,134 --> 00:23:21,904
You are one very lucky boy.

303
00:23:22,037 --> 00:23:24,573
Thank you for saving me.

304
00:23:24,706 --> 00:23:26,541
I wish I could say I did.

305
00:23:26,675 --> 00:23:29,144
But I didn't save you.

306
00:23:30,212 --> 00:23:31,914
I don't understand.

307
00:23:32,047 --> 00:23:33,715
That makes the two of us.

308
00:23:33,849 --> 00:23:36,118
But we're going
to run some tests,

309
00:23:36,251 --> 00:23:38,486
see if we can figure out
what happened.

310
00:23:38,620 --> 00:23:39,955
Sergei.

311
00:23:40,088 --> 00:23:41,223
Dima.

312
00:23:47,596 --> 00:23:49,264
NIKOLAI:
Why did you not shoot?

313
00:23:50,732 --> 00:23:53,802
You must be Sergei's father.

314
00:23:53,936 --> 00:23:55,804
Mr. Kravinoff.

315
00:23:55,938 --> 00:23:57,606
I am here to take him home.

316
00:23:57,739 --> 00:23:59,942
He needs to stay here
and recover.

317
00:24:00,075 --> 00:24:03,812
Clinically, he was dead
for more than three minutes.

318
00:24:03,946 --> 00:24:06,081
He will be leaving with me.

319
00:24:06,214 --> 00:24:09,184
[WOMAN HUMMING
"BAYU BAYUSHKI BAYU" FAINTLY]

320
00:24:10,919 --> 00:24:12,955
[DRAWER OPENS]

321
00:24:21,029 --> 00:24:22,831
MOTHER: [VOICE-OVER]
<i>Sergei...</i>

322
00:24:41,650 --> 00:24:43,719
NIKOLAI: [CALLING]
Sergei!

323
00:24:43,852 --> 00:24:45,687
Come down here!

324
00:24:50,559 --> 00:24:52,828
[IMPERSONATING NIKOLAI]
Father is the only animal

325
00:24:52,961 --> 00:24:54,296
that is dreaded.

326
00:24:54,429 --> 00:24:56,732
[LAUGHS] You're getting
too good at that.

327
00:24:56,865 --> 00:24:58,834
You'll be all right.

328
00:24:58,967 --> 00:25:01,169
You almost got
your brother killed.

329
00:25:02,637 --> 00:25:06,541
You almost got yourself killed,
because you were afraid.

330
00:25:07,609 --> 00:25:09,811
Fear will eat you.

331
00:25:11,013 --> 00:25:13,482
It makes you weak.

332
00:25:13,615 --> 00:25:15,851
Are you weak like your mother?

333
00:25:15,984 --> 00:25:17,386
Crazy?

334
00:25:17,519 --> 00:25:19,121
Or are you like me?

335
00:25:19,254 --> 00:25:22,891
Because if you show weakness
to enemies,

336
00:25:23,025 --> 00:25:26,161
it gives them an opening.

337
00:25:27,829 --> 00:25:30,399
You are old enough
to understand.

338
00:25:32,167 --> 00:25:34,636
You know my business. Yes?

339
00:25:35,871 --> 00:25:39,207
One day, you will be in charge.

340
00:25:39,341 --> 00:25:41,576
Dmitri, go.

341
00:25:41,710 --> 00:25:45,747
Dmitri will go back to school
in New York,

342
00:25:45,881 --> 00:25:48,250
and you will stay here.

343
00:25:48,383 --> 00:25:49,551
With me.

344
00:25:49,684 --> 00:25:52,721
I think America is
making you soft.

345
00:25:52,854 --> 00:25:55,424
-It is for your own good.
-[CLOCK CHIMING]

346
00:25:55,557 --> 00:25:58,560
Each of us have a path to walk.

347
00:26:00,695 --> 00:26:03,131
Embrace who you really are,

348
00:26:03,265 --> 00:26:05,501
and you will have the strength
to walk it.

349
00:26:07,969 --> 00:26:09,571
Come.

350
00:26:10,639 --> 00:26:12,674
Come here.

351
00:26:15,710 --> 00:26:17,479
I got you something.

352
00:26:24,419 --> 00:26:27,557
You never have to be
afraid again.

353
00:26:38,834 --> 00:26:40,135
He should've killed you!

354
00:26:42,505 --> 00:26:43,738
What is going on with you?

355
00:26:45,307 --> 00:26:47,676
[GASPING BREATHS]

356
00:26:47,809 --> 00:26:49,945
Sergei! Get back here!

357
00:26:51,746 --> 00:26:53,148
[DOOR SLAMS SHUT]

358
00:26:53,281 --> 00:26:56,084
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

359
00:26:56,218 --> 00:26:57,486
Are you okay?

360
00:27:01,557 --> 00:27:03,158
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

361
00:27:03,291 --> 00:27:05,293
-[BIRD CHIRPING]
-[TAPPING ON WINDOW]

362
00:27:10,298 --> 00:27:11,933
[CHIRPING]

363
00:27:19,674 --> 00:27:22,277
[WINGS FLUTTERING,
BIRD SCREECHING]

364
00:28:11,760 --> 00:28:13,629
[GASPING]

365
00:28:13,762 --> 00:28:15,297
[BREATHING RAPIDLY]

366
00:28:34,049 --> 00:28:35,283
Don't leave me with him.

367
00:28:35,417 --> 00:28:37,085
I'm going.

368
00:28:37,219 --> 00:28:39,387
-I have to.
-Why?

369
00:28:39,522 --> 00:28:42,424
I can't explain it.
Something's happened to me.

370
00:28:42,558 --> 00:28:44,059
What are you talking about?

371
00:28:44,192 --> 00:28:47,162
Do you remember the place
we used to camp?

372
00:28:47,295 --> 00:28:49,898
Where all you could hear
were the crickets and the owls?

373
00:28:50,031 --> 00:28:53,068
And Mom used to sing to us
around the fire?

374
00:28:53,201 --> 00:28:55,036
That land is all
I have left of her.

375
00:28:55,170 --> 00:28:57,939
How does that make it okay?

376
00:28:58,073 --> 00:28:59,542
Picture me there.

377
00:29:00,909 --> 00:29:02,210
[SCOFFS]

378
00:29:03,245 --> 00:29:05,113
I'm sorry, Dima.

379
00:29:05,247 --> 00:29:06,448
I am.

380
00:29:10,118 --> 00:29:12,420
Just go if you're gonna go.

381
00:29:14,690 --> 00:29:16,224
Go.

382
00:29:19,729 --> 00:29:21,597
I won't be gone forever.

383
00:29:31,006 --> 00:29:33,074
Where you headed?

384
00:29:33,208 --> 00:29:35,076
Trying to get out of England.

385
00:29:35,210 --> 00:29:36,444
To Russia.

386
00:29:36,579 --> 00:29:38,748
On this?

387
00:29:38,880 --> 00:29:41,816
You know there's planes
and trains for that, don't you?

388
00:29:43,118 --> 00:29:44,419
You on the run?

389
00:29:44,553 --> 00:29:46,388
Yes.

390
00:29:46,522 --> 00:29:47,757
I am.

391
00:29:47,889 --> 00:29:49,457
Come on, then. Come on.

392
00:29:59,234 --> 00:30:01,836
[WIND WHISTLING]

393
00:30:17,553 --> 00:30:19,622
-[SOFT RINGING IN EARS]
-[DISTANT BELLOWING]

394
00:30:22,357 --> 00:30:24,359
[GALLOPING HOOFBEATS
IN DISTANCE]

395
00:30:30,733 --> 00:30:32,867
[GALLOPING HOOFBEATS CONTINUE]

396
00:30:34,336 --> 00:30:36,971
[BELLOWING]

397
00:30:37,105 --> 00:30:39,040
[BREATHING DEEPLY]

398
00:30:39,174 --> 00:30:40,743
[THUNDERING HOOFBEATS]

399
00:30:40,875 --> 00:30:43,078
[BELLOWING]

400
00:30:50,185 --> 00:30:52,120
[BELLOWING CONTINUES]

401
00:31:02,864 --> 00:31:04,866
[BELLOWING CONTINUES]

402
00:31:15,511 --> 00:31:18,179
[SNORTING, BELLOWS]

403
00:31:21,617 --> 00:31:23,819
[BELLOWING]

404
00:31:30,826 --> 00:31:32,828
[WIND WHISTLING SOFTLY]

405
00:31:37,399 --> 00:31:40,402
[WOMAN SINGING
"BAYU BAYUSHKI BAYU" FAINTLY]

406
00:31:54,482 --> 00:31:56,451
[SINGING GROWS LOUDER]

407
00:32:00,054 --> 00:32:01,990
[SINGING CONTINUES
WITH LYRICS IN RUSSIAN]

408
00:32:12,701 --> 00:32:14,670
[DISTANT THUNDER RUMBLING]

409
00:32:16,938 --> 00:32:18,940
[SINGING CONTINUES]

410
00:32:27,015 --> 00:32:28,983
[THUNDER CRASHING]

411
00:32:29,117 --> 00:32:31,453
NIKOLAI: [VOICE-OVER]
<i>She was weak.</i>

412
00:32:31,587 --> 00:32:33,455
<i>Sick in her mind.</i>

413
00:32:33,589 --> 00:32:35,256
SERGEI: [VOICE-OVER] <i>She died</i>
<i>because you sent her away.</i>

414
00:32:35,390 --> 00:32:36,491
<i>Sergei!</i>

415
00:32:36,625 --> 00:32:38,460
-[ROARING]
<i>-Run!</i>

416
00:32:38,594 --> 00:32:41,429
-[THUNDER CRASHING]
-[ECHOING] <i>Sergei!</i>

417
00:32:41,564 --> 00:32:42,798
[BRANCH CRACKING]

418
00:32:42,932 --> 00:32:44,667
[VOICE-OVER]
<i>Fear will eat you.</i>

419
00:32:44,800 --> 00:32:47,368
<i>It makes you weak.</i>

420
00:32:47,503 --> 00:32:50,038
<i>Each of us has a path to walk.</i>

421
00:32:52,541 --> 00:32:53,909
<i>They are prey.</i>

422
00:32:54,042 --> 00:32:55,477
[GALLOPING HOOFBEATS]

423
00:32:55,611 --> 00:32:58,346
<i>We are predators.</i>

424
00:32:58,480 --> 00:33:00,381
[METALLIC RINGING]

425
00:33:00,516 --> 00:33:02,116
[BLOWS]

426
00:33:06,221 --> 00:33:07,288
[BELLOWS]

427
00:33:07,422 --> 00:33:08,591
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

428
00:33:08,724 --> 00:33:10,425
[PANTING]

429
00:33:19,935 --> 00:33:21,770
[GRUNTS]

430
00:33:25,774 --> 00:33:28,176
[PANTING, LAUGHS SOFTLY]

431
00:33:28,309 --> 00:33:30,478
[WATER RUNNING]

432
00:33:32,447 --> 00:33:35,016
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

433
00:33:35,149 --> 00:33:38,219
[DISTANT GUNSHOT ECHOING]

434
00:33:38,353 --> 00:33:40,823
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

435
00:33:40,956 --> 00:33:42,992
[GRUNTING]

436
00:33:48,463 --> 00:33:50,900
[DISTANT GUNSHOT ECHOING]

437
00:33:54,870 --> 00:33:56,304
[GASPS]

438
00:34:19,662 --> 00:34:21,630
[INSECTS BUZZING]

439
00:34:24,033 --> 00:34:26,067
[CLICKING]

440
00:34:49,892 --> 00:34:51,894
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

441
00:35:00,569 --> 00:35:03,471
[EERIE VOICES ECHOING]

442
00:35:08,510 --> 00:35:09,578
[SERGEI YELLS]

443
00:35:12,615 --> 00:35:14,583
-[GRUNTING]
-[BLOWS LANDING, CRUNCHING]

444
00:35:26,929 --> 00:35:29,865
[WOMAN SINGING
"BAYU BAYUSHKI BAYU" FAINTLY]

445
00:35:33,267 --> 00:35:35,269
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

446
00:35:55,156 --> 00:35:57,458
[SINGING FADES]

447
00:36:21,116 --> 00:36:22,685
PILOT: [OVER RADIO]
Welcome home.

448
00:36:22,818 --> 00:36:25,353
<i>We stayed under the radar</i>
<i>as usual.</i>

449
00:36:25,486 --> 00:36:27,823
<i>Call me when you need me again.</i>

450
00:36:29,124 --> 00:36:31,093
[DOORS WHIRRING OPEN]

451
00:36:41,469 --> 00:36:42,671
[GRUNTS]

452
00:36:44,272 --> 00:36:46,542
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

453
00:36:54,183 --> 00:36:56,518
[PHONE BEEPING]

454
00:36:56,652 --> 00:36:59,387
NIKOLAI: [RECORDING]
<i>Sergei, it is your father.</i>

455
00:36:59,521 --> 00:37:01,557
<i>Come home. I miss you.</i>

456
00:37:01,690 --> 00:37:04,693
<i>I am sorry for everything</i>
<i>that has happened.</i>

457
00:37:04,827 --> 00:37:06,729
-[LAUGHTER OVER PHONE]
-[SCOFFS]

458
00:37:06,862 --> 00:37:08,697
DMITRI: <i>Just kidding.</i>
<i>It's your brother.</i>

459
00:37:08,831 --> 00:37:10,431
<i>I texted you.</i>
<i>Where have you been?</i>

460
00:37:10,566 --> 00:37:11,734
[SPLASHING]

461
00:37:11,867 --> 00:37:13,434
-[GRUNTING]
-[CHUCKLES] <i>Oh.</i>

462
00:37:13,569 --> 00:37:16,237
<i>Are you still hiding out</i>
<i>in the woods, huh?</i>

463
00:37:16,370 --> 00:37:17,506
<i>Am I gonna see you</i>

464
00:37:17,639 --> 00:37:18,774
<i>-for my birthday?</i>
-Hmm.

465
00:37:18,907 --> 00:37:20,576
<i>Call me back.</i>

466
00:37:28,550 --> 00:37:30,219
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

467
00:37:33,722 --> 00:37:36,225
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

468
00:37:36,357 --> 00:37:38,326
[GROANS]

469
00:37:41,764 --> 00:37:43,866
[EXHALES HEAVILY]

470
00:37:43,999 --> 00:37:46,969
-[DISTANT GUNSHOT ECHOING]
-[MAN SPEAKING RUSSIAN]

471
00:37:53,242 --> 00:37:55,110
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER
IN RUSSIAN]

472
00:38:09,958 --> 00:38:11,827
[ENGINE IDLING]

473
00:38:31,613 --> 00:38:33,381
-Move.
-[TRUCK ENGINE REVVING]

474
00:38:39,288 --> 00:38:40,722
Because we can.

475
00:38:43,424 --> 00:38:45,194
Because you can?

476
00:38:45,326 --> 00:38:46,662
Out of the way.

477
00:38:46,795 --> 00:38:48,931
There's six of us
and only one of you.

478
00:38:49,965 --> 00:38:51,465
There are six of you now.

479
00:38:51,600 --> 00:38:53,702
I ain't got time for this.
I've got deadlines.

480
00:38:53,836 --> 00:38:55,469
[SPEAKING RUSSIAN]

481
00:38:57,005 --> 00:38:59,808
[GEARS SHIFTING,
ENGINE ACCELERATING]

482
00:39:01,977 --> 00:39:03,745
[GRUNTS]

483
00:39:08,349 --> 00:39:10,252
[GRUNTING VICIOUSLY]

484
00:39:14,156 --> 00:39:15,791
[GRUNTING]

485
00:39:17,626 --> 00:39:19,194
[SPITS]

486
00:39:20,428 --> 00:39:21,797
Go, go!

487
00:39:22,798 --> 00:39:25,466
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

488
00:39:33,474 --> 00:39:34,710
[BIRDS CAWING]

489
00:39:34,843 --> 00:39:36,712
[ENGINE IDLING]

490
00:39:36,845 --> 00:39:38,847
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

491
00:39:44,720 --> 00:39:46,021
[SIGHS]

492
00:39:53,528 --> 00:39:54,997
Mr. Tagland.

493
00:39:56,031 --> 00:39:57,666
I apologize.

494
00:39:57,799 --> 00:40:00,269
This guy,
he came out of nowhere.

495
00:40:00,401 --> 00:40:03,705
A crazy local or...

496
00:40:03,839 --> 00:40:05,540
I don't know.

497
00:40:05,674 --> 00:40:07,475
But I took care of it.

498
00:40:07,609 --> 00:40:09,244
He won't be
bothering us anymore.

499
00:40:13,181 --> 00:40:16,084
In a moment, you won't be
bothered by much of anything.

500
00:40:16,218 --> 00:40:17,953
How did you...?

501
00:40:19,021 --> 00:40:21,123
Where's Mr. Tagland?

502
00:40:21,256 --> 00:40:24,059
Oh, you're standing in him.

503
00:40:26,528 --> 00:40:28,096
Found this.

504
00:40:28,230 --> 00:40:29,765
Interesting read.

505
00:40:29,898 --> 00:40:31,400
You're a poacher.

506
00:40:31,533 --> 00:40:35,003
Mr. Tagland, he hires poachers,
but these names...

507
00:40:35,137 --> 00:40:36,838
drugs, weapons, trafficking.

508
00:40:36,972 --> 00:40:38,273
No, no, I, um...

509
00:40:38,407 --> 00:40:39,775
What's your name?

510
00:40:39,908 --> 00:40:41,475
Andre.

511
00:40:41,610 --> 00:40:43,245
Andre who?

512
00:40:43,378 --> 00:40:45,247
The-the men in that book,
they're the ones you want.

513
00:40:45,380 --> 00:40:48,050
They're the ones in charge.
I-I-I can help you find them.

514
00:40:48,183 --> 00:40:50,152
I don't need your help.

515
00:40:51,687 --> 00:40:54,256
But I will be adding
these names to my list.

516
00:40:55,524 --> 00:40:57,392
Andre who?

517
00:40:58,593 --> 00:41:00,128
Lavigne.

518
00:41:01,396 --> 00:41:03,365
Pretty low on
the pecking order, Andre.

519
00:41:03,497 --> 00:41:04,465
[SIGHS]

520
00:41:04,599 --> 00:41:06,768
Oh. Found you.

521
00:41:06,902 --> 00:41:08,437
[CRIES OUT]

522
00:41:21,249 --> 00:41:23,251
[DISTANT THUNDER RUMBLING]

523
00:41:23,385 --> 00:41:26,188
NEWSWOMAN: [OVER SPEAKER]
<i>And now, today's headlines.</i>

524
00:41:26,321 --> 00:41:28,991
<i>Crusading London prosecutor</i>
<i>Samantha Hodges</i>

525
00:41:29,124 --> 00:41:31,960
<i>was gunned down last week</i>
<i>in broad daylight</i>

526
00:41:32,094 --> 00:41:34,296
<i>following a string</i>
<i>of vicious attacks</i>

527
00:41:34,429 --> 00:41:38,133
<i>targeting law enforcement</i>
<i>and the judiciary.</i>

528
00:41:38,266 --> 00:41:41,136
<i>Memorial services</i>
<i>will be held later today.</i>

529
00:41:41,269 --> 00:41:42,571
[CLOSES LAPTOP]

530
00:41:43,839 --> 00:41:46,074
[SNIFFLES]

531
00:41:46,208 --> 00:41:50,345
CALYPSO: I met Samantha
when I first moved to London.

532
00:41:50,479 --> 00:41:53,548
She was a mentor,

533
00:41:53,682 --> 00:41:56,385
a dear friend,

534
00:41:56,518 --> 00:41:59,788
and one of the fiercest
fighters for justice

535
00:41:59,921 --> 00:42:02,190
this city has ever known.

536
00:42:04,826 --> 00:42:06,762
We all know who did this.

537
00:42:08,196 --> 00:42:12,567
Samantha dared to stand
in Semyon Chorney's way

538
00:42:12,701 --> 00:42:15,070
and hold him accountable.

539
00:42:15,203 --> 00:42:20,142
And for that act of courage,
she lost her life.

540
00:42:23,812 --> 00:42:25,847
This system's broken.

541
00:42:31,887 --> 00:42:33,889
[LOW CHATTER]

542
00:42:36,992 --> 00:42:39,394
-I'm sorry about your friend.
-Shit.

543
00:42:40,729 --> 00:42:41,963
I didn't mean to scare you.

544
00:42:42,097 --> 00:42:43,765
Well, you did.

545
00:42:43,899 --> 00:42:45,033
Sorry for your loss.

546
00:42:45,167 --> 00:42:47,135
Did you know her well?

547
00:42:47,269 --> 00:42:50,372
Actually, I didn't
know her at all.

548
00:42:50,506 --> 00:42:52,441
Well, then, thank you
for the condolences.

549
00:42:54,843 --> 00:42:56,078
Calypso.

550
00:43:05,420 --> 00:43:07,557
I think this belongs to you.

551
00:43:12,794 --> 00:43:14,396
You're...

552
00:43:15,430 --> 00:43:16,665
You're the boy.

553
00:43:18,366 --> 00:43:19,768
But no, you were...

554
00:43:19,901 --> 00:43:22,137
-You were re--
-I was.

555
00:43:22,270 --> 00:43:23,772
For three minutes.

556
00:43:23,905 --> 00:43:25,440
Would have been
a whole lot longer

557
00:43:25,575 --> 00:43:26,741
if you hadn't been there.

558
00:43:26,875 --> 00:43:29,545
Those were
my grandmother's cards.

559
00:43:29,678 --> 00:43:32,247
I actually still carry
the deck with me.

560
00:43:32,380 --> 00:43:34,584
So, why'd you give it to me?

561
00:43:35,617 --> 00:43:37,152
Guess I thought you needed it.

562
00:43:38,954 --> 00:43:40,622
This all you had to go on?

563
00:43:40,755 --> 00:43:42,090
How'd you find me?

564
00:43:44,626 --> 00:43:48,263
Hunting people down
is sort of my thing.

565
00:43:48,396 --> 00:43:49,599
Hunting?

566
00:43:49,731 --> 00:43:51,766
You know who did this?

567
00:43:53,135 --> 00:43:55,003
Yeah, I do.

568
00:43:56,271 --> 00:43:57,507
They gonna get him?

569
00:43:57,639 --> 00:43:59,841
Probably not.

570
00:44:04,446 --> 00:44:07,115
What would you say
if I told you...

571
00:44:08,450 --> 00:44:09,718
...I already did?

572
00:44:46,855 --> 00:44:48,156
A tiger's tooth?

573
00:44:48,290 --> 00:44:51,527
I use whatever tools
are available.

574
00:44:51,661 --> 00:44:53,828
Why would you do that?

575
00:44:53,962 --> 00:44:56,164
Wasn't he responsible
for killing your friend?

576
00:44:58,099 --> 00:45:03,738
Look, I've been trying to
find you for a very long time.

577
00:45:03,872 --> 00:45:06,908
This is my way of saying
thank you for saving my life.

578
00:45:07,042 --> 00:45:08,644
I didn't ask you
to murder anyone.

579
00:45:08,777 --> 00:45:10,345
I'm a lawyer.

580
00:45:13,215 --> 00:45:15,750
But that bastard got
what he deserved.

581
00:45:18,987 --> 00:45:21,022
I know who your father is.

582
00:45:22,857 --> 00:45:24,560
You're like him?

583
00:45:24,694 --> 00:45:25,794
A gangster?

584
00:45:25,927 --> 00:45:27,563
No.

585
00:45:29,898 --> 00:45:34,035
I grew up watching my father
put evil into the world.

586
00:45:34,169 --> 00:45:36,404
The old man had it
all figured out.

587
00:45:36,539 --> 00:45:38,907
I was supposed to follow
in his footsteps

588
00:45:39,040 --> 00:45:43,078
and take over
the family business.

589
00:45:43,211 --> 00:45:45,914
Something happened to me
that day you found me.

590
00:45:48,049 --> 00:45:52,887
So, I got as far away
from my father as I could.

591
00:45:54,422 --> 00:45:57,926
And now I do what I can
to get rid of people like him.

592
00:45:58,059 --> 00:46:00,563
So, you're The Hunter?

593
00:46:00,696 --> 00:46:03,131
That's just what they call me
in the press.

594
00:46:04,899 --> 00:46:06,401
I prefer Kraven.

595
00:46:06,535 --> 00:46:07,969
Kraven?

596
00:46:08,103 --> 00:46:09,404
Hmm. With a "K."

597
00:46:09,538 --> 00:46:11,273
Hmm.

598
00:46:11,406 --> 00:46:13,308
But the only people who have
heard that name are dead now.

599
00:46:13,441 --> 00:46:16,512
Then I guess I'll just
have to watch my back.

600
00:46:16,646 --> 00:46:18,446
[SERGEI LAUGHING]

601
00:46:18,581 --> 00:46:20,148
CALYPSO:
So, do you live here?

602
00:46:20,282 --> 00:46:21,850
[STAMMERS]
I live about as far away

603
00:46:21,983 --> 00:46:24,754
as you can possibly get
from this place.

604
00:46:26,388 --> 00:46:28,123
But my brother does.

605
00:46:29,725 --> 00:46:31,627
We, um...

606
00:46:31,761 --> 00:46:33,428
[SIGHS]

607
00:46:33,562 --> 00:46:36,599
I wasn't always there
for him, so I...

608
00:46:36,732 --> 00:46:38,734
check in when I can.

609
00:46:40,201 --> 00:46:41,836
What about you?

610
00:46:41,970 --> 00:46:43,805
How'd you end up here?

611
00:46:43,938 --> 00:46:45,940
Some days, I'm not so sure.

612
00:46:46,074 --> 00:46:47,275
Um...

613
00:46:48,810 --> 00:46:52,881
My parents were lawyers,
so that's what I did.

614
00:46:53,014 --> 00:46:55,518
I was in the D.A.'s office
in New York for seven years

615
00:46:55,651 --> 00:46:58,453
until I couldn't
take it anymore.

616
00:46:58,587 --> 00:47:01,156
Sometimes, the law can
get in the way of justice.

617
00:47:01,289 --> 00:47:02,991
It can.

618
00:47:05,060 --> 00:47:06,361
Now I'm in London,

619
00:47:06,494 --> 00:47:09,497
at one of the biggest law firms
in Europe.

620
00:47:09,632 --> 00:47:11,132
I know where you work.

621
00:47:11,266 --> 00:47:13,301
You're one of the best
investigative lawyers

622
00:47:13,435 --> 00:47:14,969
in that place.

623
00:47:15,103 --> 00:47:17,640
I also know...

624
00:47:17,773 --> 00:47:20,475
all your clients
aren't exactly angels.

625
00:47:20,609 --> 00:47:23,144
That's true.

626
00:47:23,278 --> 00:47:26,047
So, what are you really getting
done from behind that desk?

627
00:47:27,882 --> 00:47:29,518
I have a list.

628
00:47:29,652 --> 00:47:31,486
A list?

629
00:47:36,091 --> 00:47:37,727
There are other ways to do

630
00:47:37,859 --> 00:47:39,961
what you set out to do,
Calypso.

631
00:47:47,737 --> 00:47:49,404
[PAPER RUSTLING]

632
00:47:51,005 --> 00:47:53,408
Well, you're gonna need
a lawyer, or worse,

633
00:47:53,542 --> 00:47:55,511
if you keep messing around
in this world.

634
00:47:58,380 --> 00:48:00,716
What about a partnership?

635
00:48:00,850 --> 00:48:04,085
From inside that firm,
you can find people I can't.

636
00:48:04,219 --> 00:48:06,722
-And then I could do what...
-Yeah, I get it.

637
00:48:11,459 --> 00:48:12,661
I'll think about it.

638
00:48:14,028 --> 00:48:15,330
Kraven.

639
00:48:15,463 --> 00:48:18,099
And a little friendly advice.

640
00:48:18,233 --> 00:48:21,102
If you keep going after
the names on that list,

641
00:48:21,236 --> 00:48:24,406
people you care about
are gonna get hurt.

642
00:48:30,412 --> 00:48:32,213
[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]

643
00:48:34,482 --> 00:48:36,752
ALEKSEI:
Hey. Raja.

644
00:48:36,886 --> 00:48:38,453
We need to talk about this.

645
00:48:38,587 --> 00:48:40,922
-Yes. We go again?
-[RAJA PANTING]

646
00:48:41,055 --> 00:48:42,357
Go. Go.

647
00:48:44,560 --> 00:48:47,462
[GASPING FOR BREATH]

648
00:48:47,596 --> 00:48:49,665
-Did you hear me?
-[BREATHLESSLY] Raja.

649
00:48:49,799 --> 00:48:51,132
Raja.

650
00:48:51,266 --> 00:48:53,168
Come on, give it here.

651
00:48:53,301 --> 00:48:55,604
Oh, you're going
to make me beg?

652
00:48:57,873 --> 00:48:59,307
You know I don't beg.

653
00:49:00,609 --> 00:49:02,611
You think I'm weak?

654
00:49:04,513 --> 00:49:06,448
-Give me the damn thing.
-[GROWLING]

655
00:49:06,582 --> 00:49:09,217
[GROWLING CONTINUES]

656
00:49:09,350 --> 00:49:11,085
-Raja!
-[WHINES]

657
00:49:11,219 --> 00:49:13,556
It's okay, Ryazhenka. Yes.

658
00:49:13,689 --> 00:49:15,624
You're my... [SPEAKS RUSSIAN]

659
00:49:15,758 --> 00:49:17,292
Papa loves you.

660
00:49:17,425 --> 00:49:18,928
Papa forgives you.

661
00:49:19,060 --> 00:49:20,529
One more thing.

662
00:49:20,663 --> 00:49:23,298
Semyon Chorney was killed
in his prison cell.

663
00:49:25,133 --> 00:49:26,468
Who got to him?

664
00:49:26,602 --> 00:49:28,470
They're saying
it was The Hunter.

665
00:49:29,505 --> 00:49:31,473
Faster than a cheetah.

666
00:49:31,607 --> 00:49:33,843
Cunning as a fox.

667
00:49:33,975 --> 00:49:36,946
More ferocious than a tiger.

668
00:49:37,078 --> 00:49:40,683
[LAUGHING]

669
00:49:40,816 --> 00:49:46,454
Tell me, do you think
this Hunter actually exists?

670
00:49:46,589 --> 00:49:48,791
Could be a load of bollocks.

671
00:49:48,924 --> 00:49:51,125
But then again,
I hear he's got a list.

672
00:49:51,259 --> 00:49:54,295
Once you're on it,
you never come off.

673
00:49:56,297 --> 00:49:58,667
And there's a good chance
you're on it.

674
00:50:02,170 --> 00:50:05,708
If he is real, he can be found.

675
00:50:06,775 --> 00:50:08,944
I'll do some digging.

676
00:50:09,077 --> 00:50:11,479
Wait.

677
00:50:11,614 --> 00:50:15,316
Chorney's operations
are up for grabs, no?

678
00:50:15,450 --> 00:50:17,118
Set a meet.

679
00:50:18,152 --> 00:50:20,221
His top three guys.

680
00:50:20,355 --> 00:50:22,357
[ENGINES REVVING]

681
00:50:42,945 --> 00:50:47,048
Your boss, Semyon Chorney,
is dead.

682
00:50:47,181 --> 00:50:51,352
I intend to assume control
of his asset transactions.

683
00:50:51,486 --> 00:50:53,722
One of you will be my partner.

684
00:50:53,856 --> 00:50:55,724
Who's it going to be?

685
00:50:55,858 --> 00:50:57,225
[CHUCKLING SOFTLY]

686
00:50:57,358 --> 00:50:58,459
The best pitch wins.

687
00:51:02,531 --> 00:51:07,536
But don't you want to know
why they call me The Rhino?

688
00:51:10,371 --> 00:51:12,373
[SOFT HISSING]

689
00:51:14,309 --> 00:51:15,744
Why do it to yourself?

690
00:51:17,513 --> 00:51:19,515
They have to see
who they're dealing with.

691
00:51:22,317 --> 00:51:24,118
[SKIN CRACKLING]

692
00:51:28,724 --> 00:51:31,159
[CRACKLING CONTINUES]

693
00:51:36,732 --> 00:51:38,466
[RAJA WHINING]

694
00:51:40,069 --> 00:51:41,537
Oh, it's okay, Raja.

695
00:51:41,670 --> 00:51:43,639
It's okay.

696
00:51:43,772 --> 00:51:45,273
[EXHALES]

697
00:51:47,208 --> 00:51:49,210
[GRUNTS]

698
00:51:49,344 --> 00:51:51,212
[SIGHS]

699
00:52:00,723 --> 00:52:02,323
[GRUNTS]

700
00:52:08,931 --> 00:52:10,599
[SKIN CRACKLING]

701
00:52:13,368 --> 00:52:15,470
[SIGHS HEAVILY]

702
00:52:15,604 --> 00:52:17,673
[CRACKLING SUBSIDES]

703
00:52:19,808 --> 00:52:22,477
[GRUNTING]

704
00:52:22,611 --> 00:52:24,479
You can put your guns away.

705
00:52:24,613 --> 00:52:27,215
If I want you dead,
I only have to raise my...

706
00:52:27,348 --> 00:52:28,617
Don't.

707
00:52:31,120 --> 00:52:34,123
When a rhino sees
his opportunity,

708
00:52:34,255 --> 00:52:36,025
he doesn't hesitate.

709
00:52:37,158 --> 00:52:39,662
He charges in and takes it.

710
00:52:39,795 --> 00:52:42,463
So, I'll ask one more time.

711
00:52:44,133 --> 00:52:46,135
Which one of you
is going to be my partner?

712
00:52:47,301 --> 00:52:48,971
-[GRUNTS]
-[GUNSHOT ECHOES]

713
00:52:51,840 --> 00:52:53,509
Hell of a pitch.

714
00:52:57,079 --> 00:52:58,881
We have a winner.

715
00:52:59,014 --> 00:53:01,583
[ALEKSEI LAUGHING]

716
00:53:01,717 --> 00:53:03,719
[PIANO PLAYING
"SIGN OF THE TIMES"]

717
00:53:11,292 --> 00:53:13,829
[IMPERSONATING HARRY STYLES]
<i>♪ Just stop your crying ♪</i>

718
00:53:13,962 --> 00:53:15,731
<i>♪ It's a sign of the times ♪</i>

719
00:53:17,432 --> 00:53:20,969
<i>♪ Welcome to the final show ♪</i>

720
00:53:21,103 --> 00:53:24,372
<i>♪ Hope you're wearing</i>
<i>your best clothes ♪</i>

721
00:53:24,506 --> 00:53:26,909
[LOW CROWD CHATTER]

722
00:53:27,042 --> 00:53:31,613
<i>♪ You can't bribe the door</i>
<i>on your way to the sky ♪</i>

723
00:53:33,749 --> 00:53:37,218
<i>♪ You look pretty good</i>
<i>down here ♪</i>

724
00:53:37,351 --> 00:53:39,621
<i>♪ But you ain't really good ♪</i>

725
00:53:43,692 --> 00:53:45,594
[SONG ENDS]

726
00:53:45,728 --> 00:53:47,596
[SCATTERED APPLAUSE]

727
00:53:47,730 --> 00:53:49,397
My son Dmitri.

728
00:53:50,699 --> 00:53:54,103
This next one's for you, Papa.

729
00:53:54,235 --> 00:53:56,337
[PLAYING "THEY CAN'T
TAKE THAT AWAY FROM ME"]

730
00:53:56,471 --> 00:53:58,339
[IMPERSONATING TONY BENNETT]
<i>♪ The way ♪</i>

731
00:53:58,473 --> 00:54:00,341
<i>♪ You wear your hat... ♪</i>

732
00:54:00,475 --> 00:54:01,910
[CHUCKLES]
He does for me.

733
00:54:02,044 --> 00:54:03,746
He knows I like Tony Bennett.

734
00:54:03,879 --> 00:54:05,480
Do you like Tony Bennett?

735
00:54:05,614 --> 00:54:08,416
I don't trust anyone
who doesn't like Tony Bennett.

736
00:54:08,550 --> 00:54:09,985
<i>♪ The memory of all that... ♪</i>

737
00:54:10,119 --> 00:54:13,387
He can do anyone.
He's like chameleon.

738
00:54:13,522 --> 00:54:16,658
<i>♪ They can't take that</i>
<i>away from me... ♪</i>

739
00:54:16,792 --> 00:54:22,064
These assassins, if they can
get to your boss in cage,

740
00:54:22,197 --> 00:54:24,933
I think we all need
to take precautions.

741
00:54:25,067 --> 00:54:26,201
I understand.

742
00:54:26,334 --> 00:54:28,070
Hmm. Come closer.

743
00:54:30,739 --> 00:54:34,009
Chorney, he is gone.

744
00:54:34,143 --> 00:54:37,946
That makes your operations
become vulnerable.

745
00:54:39,648 --> 00:54:43,317
I can offer you security,
distribution,

746
00:54:43,451 --> 00:54:47,421
and most critically,
peace of mind.

747
00:54:47,556 --> 00:54:49,457
Sounds good. I'm on board.

748
00:54:51,527 --> 00:54:53,494
Just like that?

749
00:54:53,629 --> 00:54:55,164
You don't want
to think about it?

750
00:54:55,296 --> 00:54:57,431
-Order has to be restored.
-[NIKOLAI CHUCKLES]

751
00:54:57,566 --> 00:54:58,901
The sooner, the better.

752
00:54:59,034 --> 00:55:01,937
[NIKOLAI CHUCKLES]

753
00:55:02,070 --> 00:55:05,473
You have already done deal,
didn't you?

754
00:55:05,607 --> 00:55:07,142
Who with?

755
00:55:07,276 --> 00:55:09,144
The Rhino sends his regards.

756
00:55:10,746 --> 00:55:12,514
-[GRUNTING]
-[PATRONS SCREAMING]

757
00:55:15,684 --> 00:55:17,351
[WHIMPERING]

758
00:55:17,485 --> 00:55:19,121
[GRUNTING]

759
00:55:20,088 --> 00:55:21,455
[WHIMPERING]

760
00:55:29,798 --> 00:55:31,266
[PANICKED SHOUTING, SCREAMING]

761
00:55:32,601 --> 00:55:34,468
[SCREAMING FADES]

762
00:55:34,603 --> 00:55:36,505
[GLASS CLATTERS UNDER FEET]

763
00:55:38,941 --> 00:55:40,809
[DMITRI WHIMPERING]

764
00:55:40,943 --> 00:55:43,011
Get up.

765
00:55:44,546 --> 00:55:47,348
[BREATHING RAGGEDLY]

766
00:56:00,095 --> 00:56:02,064
You're hit.

767
00:56:03,332 --> 00:56:04,800
Are you all right, Papa?

768
00:56:08,369 --> 00:56:10,606
[BOTTLE CLATTERS ON FLOOR]

769
00:56:10,739 --> 00:56:13,374
Look at what they have done
to my club.

770
00:56:16,144 --> 00:56:19,348
I get attacked
on my own ground...

771
00:56:21,350 --> 00:56:23,852
...and who do I have
to defend me?

772
