1030
01:12:48,469 --> 01:12:49,605
Pay them.

1031
01:12:49,738 --> 01:12:51,673
It is complicated.

1032
01:12:51,807 --> 01:12:54,676
No, it's not. It's very simple.

1033
01:12:54,810 --> 01:12:57,279
You have the money,
and he's your son.

1034
01:12:57,411 --> 01:12:59,281
This is not about money.

1035
01:12:59,413 --> 01:13:01,449
This is about power.

1036
01:13:04,720 --> 01:13:08,290
If I pay, I am weak.

1037
01:13:08,422 --> 01:13:10,192
If I show weakness,

1038
01:13:10,325 --> 01:13:14,062
I begin to lose everything
I've spent lifetime building.

1039
01:13:14,196 --> 01:13:16,598
A lifetime building what?

1040
01:13:17,866 --> 01:13:20,002
You're a drug dealer.

1041
01:13:21,536 --> 01:13:23,705
[GROWLING SIGH]

1042
01:13:23,839 --> 01:13:25,908
You don't get
to do that anymore.

1043
01:13:27,009 --> 01:13:28,710
Dmitri is innocent.

1044
01:13:28,844 --> 01:13:31,947
You let him die,
his blood is on your hands.

1045
01:13:32,080 --> 01:13:34,182
On my hands?

1046
01:13:34,316 --> 01:13:35,684
My hands?

1047
01:13:35,817 --> 01:13:38,720
I did not abandon him.

1048
01:13:38,854 --> 01:13:41,757
You abandoned him.

1049
01:13:42,824 --> 01:13:44,192
You.

1050
01:13:47,129 --> 01:13:50,132
He was dead
the moment he was taken.

1051
01:13:50,265 --> 01:13:52,401
Whether I pay or not.

1052
01:13:53,969 --> 01:13:56,571
No, you do--
You don't know that.

1053
01:13:56,705 --> 01:13:59,141
Yes, I know.

1054
01:14:00,409 --> 01:14:02,443
Because that is
what I would do.

1055
01:14:02,577 --> 01:14:04,646
You're despicable.

1056
01:14:04,780 --> 01:14:06,815
Of course I want him back.

1057
01:14:07,883 --> 01:14:10,752
I want both my sons back.

1058
01:14:13,422 --> 01:14:14,589
[SIGHS]

1059
01:14:14,723 --> 01:14:16,625
[CHUCKLES WRYLY]

1060
01:14:18,093 --> 01:14:21,063
Some legend you've become.

1061
01:14:23,799 --> 01:14:25,267
Wake up.

1062
01:14:25,400 --> 01:14:26,902
[DMITRI PANTING]

1063
01:14:27,035 --> 01:14:28,503
-[PILLS RATTLING]
-Take these.

1064
01:14:28,637 --> 01:14:30,906
-[GROANS]
-Antibiotics.

1065
01:14:31,039 --> 01:14:33,442
I can't have you dying
on me, can I?

1066
01:14:42,951 --> 01:14:45,620
[IMPERSONATING ÖMER] Can't
have you dying on me, can I?

1067
01:14:46,955 --> 01:14:48,790
[BOTTLE CLATTERING]

1068
01:14:49,791 --> 01:14:51,293
[LAUGHS SOFTLY]

1069
01:14:51,426 --> 01:14:52,728
That's good.

1070
01:14:52,861 --> 01:14:53,829
[SNIFFING]

1071
01:14:53,962 --> 01:14:55,364
[GRUNTS]

1072
01:14:59,334 --> 01:15:01,403
[PILLS RATTLING]

1073
01:15:22,090 --> 01:15:24,026
Ömer Ozdemir.

1074
01:15:24,159 --> 01:15:27,662
He's holed up in a monastery
in the outskirts of Ankara.

1075
01:15:27,796 --> 01:15:29,464
Thank you.

1076
01:15:29,598 --> 01:15:31,533
You can thank me
by never calling me again.

1077
01:15:31,666 --> 01:15:33,869
We'll see.

1078
01:15:41,276 --> 01:15:42,744
THE FOREIGNER:
How'd it go?

1079
01:15:45,147 --> 01:15:46,648
She took it.

1080
01:15:46,782 --> 01:15:48,016
Of course she took it.

1081
01:15:48,150 --> 01:15:50,585
But did she believe you?

1082
01:15:50,719 --> 01:15:52,220
Yeah. She trusts me.

1083
01:15:52,354 --> 01:15:53,855
Hmm.

1084
01:15:53,989 --> 01:15:57,192
Which is why I want double
what your boss promised.

1085
01:15:57,325 --> 01:15:59,094
Double?

1086
01:15:59,227 --> 01:16:01,063
Why not triple?

1087
01:16:01,196 --> 01:16:02,532
What game are you playing?

1088
01:16:02,664 --> 01:16:04,132
[THE FOREIGNER LAUGHS SOFTLY]

1089
01:16:06,268 --> 01:16:08,270
[ECHOING]
One.

1090
01:16:09,539 --> 01:16:11,273
[ECHOING]
Two.

1091
01:16:11,406 --> 01:16:12,741
[ECHOING]
Three.

1092
01:16:12,874 --> 01:16:14,576
-[PHONE RINGING]
-[GUNSHOT OVER PHONE]

1093
01:16:14,709 --> 01:16:16,945
It's done.

1094
01:16:20,382 --> 01:16:22,417
[SPEED DIAL TONES BEEPING]

1095
01:16:22,552 --> 01:16:24,520
[LINE RINGING]

1096
01:16:27,022 --> 01:16:28,123
[LINE CLICKS]

1097
01:16:28,256 --> 01:16:30,225
Get ready.

1098
01:16:30,358 --> 01:16:34,029
The Hunter is on his way.

1099
01:16:34,162 --> 01:16:36,731
CALYPSO: [OVER PHONE] <i>Sergei,</i>
<i>the man you're looking for</i>

1100
01:16:36,865 --> 01:16:38,733
<i>is Ömer Ozdemir.</i>

1101
01:16:38,867 --> 01:16:42,404
I found an old monastery
in his family name in Turkey.

1102
01:16:42,538 --> 01:16:46,374
And that is where
you'll find your brother.

1103
01:16:46,509 --> 01:16:48,777
Thank you for this.

1104
01:16:48,910 --> 01:16:51,313
-[ENGINE IDLING]
-All right, Ellie, let's go.

1105
01:16:58,487 --> 01:17:00,489
[STRAINED GRUNTING]

1106
01:17:05,460 --> 01:17:07,462
[MEN SPEAKING TURKISH NEARBY]

1107
01:17:09,831 --> 01:17:11,299
[HINGES CREAKING]

1108
01:17:13,503 --> 01:17:15,437
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1109
01:17:23,211 --> 01:17:25,013
[MAN SPEAKING TURKISH
OVER RADIO]

1110
01:17:30,485 --> 01:17:31,953
-[BLOWS]
-[BODYGUARD GRUNTS]

1111
01:17:32,087 --> 01:17:33,188
[GASPING]

1112
01:17:33,321 --> 01:17:34,524
[GRUNTS]

1113
01:17:36,258 --> 01:17:38,326
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1114
01:17:47,169 --> 01:17:49,104
[DISTANT BANGING]

1115
01:17:54,610 --> 01:17:56,978
-[BLOWS]
-[CLATTERING]

1116
01:18:00,282 --> 01:18:02,150
[BODYGUARDS SPEAKING TURKISH]

1117
01:18:16,164 --> 01:18:18,166
[BODYGUARDS CONTINUE
SPEAKING TURKISH]

1118
01:18:24,906 --> 01:18:26,509
[DOOR CLOSES]

1119
01:18:31,446 --> 01:18:33,415
[SPEAKING TURKISH]

1120
01:18:44,226 --> 01:18:47,162
[BODYGUARD CONTINUES
SPEAKING TURKISH]

1121
01:18:49,699 --> 01:18:51,534
-[GRUNTS, SCREAMS]
-[SHARP POP]

1122
01:18:51,667 --> 01:18:52,767
[BODYGUARDS EXCLAIMING]

1123
01:18:52,901 --> 01:18:55,170
[BODYGUARD SPEAKING TURKISH]

1124
01:18:57,272 --> 01:18:58,773
It's him.

1125
01:18:59,941 --> 01:19:01,910
[BODYGUARD SPEAKING TURKISH]

1126
01:19:04,946 --> 01:19:06,214
[BODYGUARD SCREAMING]

1127
01:19:06,348 --> 01:19:07,916
[GRUNTING]

1128
01:19:09,784 --> 01:19:11,119
[CRIES OUT]

1129
01:19:12,387 --> 01:19:14,389
[BODYGUARD SCREAMING]

1130
01:19:17,192 --> 01:19:19,027
[AUTOMATIC GUNFIRE]

1131
01:19:19,160 --> 01:19:20,161
He's there.

1132
01:19:24,766 --> 01:19:26,401
[BODYGUARDS CRYING OUT]

1133
01:19:27,135 --> 01:19:28,638
Where's Dmitri?!

1134
01:19:28,770 --> 01:19:30,138
[YELLING]

1135
01:19:31,206 --> 01:19:33,108
[ÖMER GASPING]

1136
01:19:33,241 --> 01:19:35,410
Where is he?

1137
01:19:35,544 --> 01:19:38,780
Drop me and you'll never
find your brother...

1138
01:19:38,913 --> 01:19:40,215
Kraven.

1139
01:19:44,386 --> 01:19:46,321
[WHOOSHING]

1140
01:19:47,289 --> 01:19:49,491
[ÖMER SCREAMING]

1141
01:19:57,966 --> 01:19:59,334
[PAINED GRUNTING]

1142
01:20:05,641 --> 01:20:07,510
How do you know my name?!

1143
01:20:07,643 --> 01:20:09,044
Who set me up?!

1144
01:20:09,177 --> 01:20:11,112
Who took my brother?!

1145
01:20:12,180 --> 01:20:13,549
The Rhino.

1146
01:20:13,683 --> 01:20:15,450
He's killed us both now.

1147
01:20:15,584 --> 01:20:17,385
[RUMBLING]

1148
01:20:19,655 --> 01:20:21,356
[GRUNTING]

1149
01:20:23,458 --> 01:20:25,193
[GRUNTING]

1150
01:20:30,899 --> 01:20:32,867
[POLICEMEN SPEAKING TURKISH
IN OTHER ROOM]

1151
01:20:38,173 --> 01:20:39,874
[POLICEMEN CONTINUE
SPEAKING TURKISH]

1152
01:20:40,008 --> 01:20:41,476
POLICEMAN:
Hey.

1153
01:20:48,450 --> 01:20:51,152
This is crushed rosary peas.

1154
01:20:52,688 --> 01:20:55,457
The man who did this
knows his toxins.

1155
01:20:57,258 --> 01:20:59,562
[ECHOING]
One.

1156
01:20:59,695 --> 01:21:01,329
[ECHOING]
Two.

1157
01:21:03,398 --> 01:21:05,200
[ECHOING]
Three.

1158
01:21:07,636 --> 01:21:09,270
What are you doing?

1159
01:21:10,840 --> 01:21:12,608
[CHOKING]

1160
01:21:12,742 --> 01:21:14,744
-[GASPING]
-Be seeing you.

1161
01:21:16,177 --> 01:21:17,513
[BODY THUDS]

1162
01:21:18,814 --> 01:21:20,549
[RAJA BARKING]

1163
01:21:20,683 --> 01:21:23,385
-[SNAPS FINGERS]
-That's enough, Raja.

1164
01:21:23,519 --> 01:21:26,121
Ah, hmm. I'm very sorry
about your finger.

1165
01:21:26,254 --> 01:21:27,922
Collateral damage.

1166
01:21:28,056 --> 01:21:29,891
-[BARKS]
-Cut him free.

1167
01:21:30,024 --> 01:21:31,426
[RAJA PANTING]

1168
01:21:35,163 --> 01:21:38,868
We met once,
on your father's hunting trip.

1169
01:21:39,000 --> 01:21:42,036
DMITRI:
I, uh, don't remember.

1170
01:21:42,170 --> 01:21:43,572
No, you wouldn't.

1171
01:21:43,706 --> 01:21:45,875
My hair was different.

1172
01:21:46,007 --> 01:21:47,710
You were very young.

1173
01:21:47,843 --> 01:21:49,545
Me?

1174
01:21:51,045 --> 01:21:53,014
I never forgot.

1175
01:21:55,183 --> 01:21:57,919
So, have you spoken
to my father?

1176
01:21:58,052 --> 01:22:00,723
Has he agreed to pay?

1177
01:22:00,856 --> 01:22:02,591
[LAUGHING]
No.

1178
01:22:02,725 --> 01:22:05,761
Nikolai Kravinoff was never
going to hand over $20 million

1179
01:22:05,895 --> 01:22:07,962
to get his bastard son back.

1180
01:22:09,865 --> 01:22:12,902
You're an accident, Dmitri.

1181
01:22:14,235 --> 01:22:16,906
You came into this world
as an accident,

1182
01:22:17,038 --> 01:22:20,843
and you came into my possession
as an accident.

1183
01:22:20,975 --> 01:22:22,511
So, can I go?

1184
01:22:22,645 --> 01:22:27,081
Those men who took you,
they weren't there for you.

1185
01:22:27,215 --> 01:22:29,117
They were there
for your brother.

1186
01:22:29,250 --> 01:22:30,786
Sergei?

1187
01:22:30,920 --> 01:22:34,122
Both of you went in,
but when my guys got up there--

1188
01:22:34,255 --> 01:22:36,424
poof-- he'd vanished.

1189
01:22:36,559 --> 01:22:39,194
As he always does.

1190
01:22:39,327 --> 01:22:41,229
So, I took you.

1191
01:22:41,362 --> 01:22:42,497
I got lucky.

1192
01:22:42,631 --> 01:22:44,999
Why would you ever want Sergei?

1193
01:22:45,133 --> 01:22:46,602
He never hurt anyone.

1194
01:22:46,735 --> 01:22:48,436
You really don't know, do you?

1195
01:22:48,571 --> 01:22:49,805
Know what?

1196
01:22:55,611 --> 01:22:57,111
ALEKSEI:
Wait for the end.

1197
01:22:57,245 --> 01:22:59,247
That's the best part.

1198
01:23:10,693 --> 01:23:12,126
DMITRI:
Kraven?

1199
01:23:12,260 --> 01:23:14,864
Apparently, that's what
he calls himself now.

1200
01:23:14,996 --> 01:23:18,333
You think my brother Sergei
is The Hunter?

1201
01:23:18,466 --> 01:23:20,335
The Hunter is a story.

1202
01:23:20,468 --> 01:23:22,671
A fable to put fear
into criminals.

1203
01:23:22,805 --> 01:23:25,240
Clearly, you didn't know
your brother very well.

1204
01:23:25,373 --> 01:23:27,510
What do you mean "didn't"?

1205
01:23:27,643 --> 01:23:29,410
Kraven had a list.

1206
01:23:29,545 --> 01:23:31,881
Once you're on it,
you never come off.

1207
01:23:39,420 --> 01:23:41,657
So, I went after him first.

1208
01:23:41,790 --> 01:23:43,659
[ROCKS CLATTERING]

1209
01:23:52,166 --> 01:23:53,969
Let me record this.

1210
01:23:55,771 --> 01:23:57,640
We've got Kraven.

1211
01:23:59,942 --> 01:24:02,343
Eh, I don't know about that.

1212
01:24:02,477 --> 01:24:04,078
[PAINED GRUNTING]

1213
01:24:07,115 --> 01:24:08,383
-[BONE SNAPS]
-[GRUNTS]

1214
01:24:13,421 --> 01:24:15,123
[PHONE VIBRATING]

1215
01:24:15,256 --> 01:24:16,759
[PHONE BEEPS]

1216
01:24:16,892 --> 01:24:18,627
-Hello?
-SERGEI: <i>Calypso, it's me.</i>

1217
01:24:18,761 --> 01:24:21,964
The whole thing was a trap.
The Rhino, he knows who I am.

1218
01:24:22,096 --> 01:24:24,465
<i>-He'll be after you next.</i>
-Sergei, what are you...?

1219
01:24:24,600 --> 01:24:26,267
Shit.

1220
01:24:26,401 --> 01:24:28,269
There are five guys walking
into my building right now

1221
01:24:28,403 --> 01:24:30,138
who do not look like
they belong here.

1222
01:24:30,271 --> 01:24:31,874
<i>You need to get</i>
<i>out of there now.</i>

1223
01:24:32,007 --> 01:24:33,742
<i>Get to the cargo terminal</i>
<i>at Stansted.</i>

1224
01:24:33,876 --> 01:24:35,711
<i>I'll have someone</i>
<i>meet you there.</i>

1225
01:25:03,005 --> 01:25:05,239
I call this my feed bag.

1226
01:25:07,042 --> 01:25:12,113
It's a mixture of medications
to manage my condition.

1227
01:25:12,246 --> 01:25:13,949
What happened to you?

1228
01:25:14,083 --> 01:25:16,250
I was underestimated, too.

1229
01:25:16,384 --> 01:25:17,620
In and out of hospitals.

1230
01:25:17,753 --> 01:25:20,188
They never quite knew
what was wrong.

1231
01:25:20,321 --> 01:25:24,927
I knew I would never have
your father's respect...

1232
01:25:25,060 --> 01:25:29,464
or anyone else's,
until I was strong.

1233
01:25:30,498 --> 01:25:32,801
I tried everything.

1234
01:25:32,935 --> 01:25:34,703
-And then...
-[ZIPPER WHIZZING]

1235
01:25:36,337 --> 01:25:38,707
...I found someone.

1236
01:25:38,841 --> 01:25:41,175
In New York,

1237
01:25:41,309 --> 01:25:45,581
a biochemist, a professor,
Miles Warren.

1238
01:25:45,714 --> 01:25:48,984
He was developing a procedure

1239
01:25:49,118 --> 01:25:53,022
to increase strength, tenfold.

1240
01:25:54,990 --> 01:25:57,191
I signed up on the spot.

1241
01:26:02,798 --> 01:26:06,035
My skin, it started to harden.

1242
01:26:06,167 --> 01:26:10,973
-[SKIN CRACKLING]
-I was indestructible,

1243
01:26:11,106 --> 01:26:13,174
like a rhino.

1244
01:26:14,275 --> 01:26:16,712
[STRAINING]
But the pain...

1245
01:26:19,347 --> 01:26:20,883
...it was too much.

1246
01:26:30,191 --> 01:26:32,061
[INHALES]

1247
01:26:38,232 --> 01:26:40,169
[SIGHS]

1248
01:26:40,301 --> 01:26:44,740
I think there is an animal
in each one of us, Dmitri.

1249
01:26:46,608 --> 01:26:49,011
I'm taking over
your father's territory.

1250
01:26:49,144 --> 01:26:51,146
I want you to be my partner.

1251
01:26:52,614 --> 01:26:55,249
The Kravinoff name
still opens a lot of doors,

1252
01:26:55,383 --> 01:26:58,252
and you'll finally get
the consideration you deserve.

1253
01:26:59,955 --> 01:27:01,824
You're right.

1254
01:27:02,891 --> 01:27:05,226
I have been underestimated.

1255
01:27:06,695 --> 01:27:08,197
My whole life.

1256
01:27:13,569 --> 01:27:17,405
But if you think
I'm gonna betray my family,

1257
01:27:17,539 --> 01:27:19,108
you're wrong.

1258
01:27:26,380 --> 01:27:28,217
[GUN RACKS]

1259
01:27:28,349 --> 01:27:30,886
Boss, the boys haven't
checked in.

1260
01:27:31,019 --> 01:27:32,721
I can't reach 'em.

1261
01:27:38,093 --> 01:27:39,895
Kraven is alive.

1262
01:27:40,028 --> 01:27:41,429
Hey, Bert!

1263
01:27:43,031 --> 01:27:45,266
Alpha team, Bravo team.

1264
01:27:46,300 --> 01:27:47,569
He's here.

1265
01:27:47,703 --> 01:27:49,370
-[ELEVATOR BELL DINGS]
-[RAJA BARKING]

1266
01:27:49,505 --> 01:27:52,440
[BELL CONTINUES DINGING]

1267
01:27:52,574 --> 01:27:55,210
[SNARLING, BARKING]

1268
01:27:58,446 --> 01:28:00,949
[BELL CONTINUES DINGING]

1269
01:28:01,083 --> 01:28:04,485
[WHISTLING JAUNTY TUNE]

1270
01:28:08,123 --> 01:28:10,391
[WHOOSHING]

1271
01:28:13,427 --> 01:28:15,429
[WHOOSHING]

1272
01:28:26,440 --> 01:28:28,277
[RAJA PANTING]

1273
01:28:33,515 --> 01:28:34,616
Cute.

1274
01:28:34,750 --> 01:28:37,286
Will your trick still work

1275
01:28:37,418 --> 01:28:39,555
when I remove your eyeballs
from your head?

1276
01:28:40,622 --> 01:28:42,024
Relax.

1277
01:28:46,360 --> 01:28:48,329
[ENGINE WHIRRING LOUDLY]

1278
01:28:54,603 --> 01:28:56,872
I'm sorry I got you
wrapped up in all this.

1279
01:28:57,005 --> 01:28:59,541
-Any word on Dmitri?
-Not yet.

1280
01:28:59,675 --> 01:29:01,543
Three of my sources
have gone offline

1281
01:29:01,677 --> 01:29:03,712
while tracking
The Rhino's plane.

1282
01:29:03,846 --> 01:29:07,448
I don't like
the feel of this at all.

1283
01:29:08,517 --> 01:29:10,686
CALYPSO:
So, what is this place?

1284
01:29:10,819 --> 01:29:14,223
SERGEI: My mother's family
used to own this property.

1285
01:29:14,355 --> 01:29:17,893
Well, it's really the only
thing I have left from her.

1286
01:29:22,496 --> 01:29:24,199
What is happening right now?

1287
01:29:24,333 --> 01:29:27,069
We're being hunted.

1288
01:29:27,202 --> 01:29:29,071
By who?

1289
01:29:30,371 --> 01:29:31,773
[VICIOUS ROARING]

1290
01:29:31,907 --> 01:29:33,609
[GRUNTING]

1291
01:29:35,544 --> 01:29:37,679
[SNARLING]

1292
01:29:38,714 --> 01:29:40,448
[GRUNTING]

1293
01:29:42,751 --> 01:29:44,452
[BOTH GROWLING]

1294
01:29:46,188 --> 01:29:47,388
[PANTING]

1295
01:29:49,490 --> 01:29:51,526
-[GRUNTING]
-[ROARS]

1296
01:29:51,660 --> 01:29:53,262
You don't hunt me.

1297
01:29:53,427 --> 01:29:55,030
-[HISSING]
-Yeah, get pissed.

1298
01:29:55,163 --> 01:29:57,232
What are you gonna do?
Come on, show me.

1299
01:29:57,366 --> 01:29:59,601
[BOTH GROWLING]

1300
01:30:00,869 --> 01:30:02,871
[SNARLING]

1301
01:30:07,042 --> 01:30:09,211
I've seen her around
since she was a cub,

1302
01:30:09,344 --> 01:30:11,680
but she's a lot bigger
than I remember.

1303
01:30:11,813 --> 01:30:13,782
Oh, you're a goddamn lunatic.

1304
01:30:13,916 --> 01:30:15,117
I swear.

1305
01:30:15,250 --> 01:30:17,619
Oh, you just
figure that out now?

1306
01:30:17,753 --> 01:30:21,890
I know I hired you for the job,

1307
01:30:22,024 --> 01:30:23,491
but what is Kraven to you?

1308
01:30:23,625 --> 01:30:25,459
Why the obsession?

1309
01:30:25,594 --> 01:30:27,629
My mentor was one of
the greatest assassins

1310
01:30:27,763 --> 01:30:28,931
who ever lived.

1311
01:30:29,064 --> 01:30:31,133
He taught me everything I know.

1312
01:30:31,266 --> 01:30:32,801
He was like a brother to me.

1313
01:30:32,935 --> 01:30:35,237
Maybe you knew him?

1314
01:30:35,370 --> 01:30:37,005
Hmm. Of him.

1315
01:30:39,541 --> 01:30:41,176
He was murdered.

1316
01:30:41,310 --> 01:30:44,513
One man made it inside
and cut his throat.

1317
01:30:44,646 --> 01:30:46,415
Kraven?

1318
01:30:47,883 --> 01:30:50,484
So, I traveled the world,

1319
01:30:50,619 --> 01:30:53,188
followed him wherever he went.

1320
01:30:53,322 --> 01:30:56,224
But Kraven is
nature's perfect predator.

1321
01:30:56,358 --> 01:30:58,894
He has no known weaknesses.

1322
01:30:59,027 --> 01:31:01,462
[BREATHES DEEPLY]

1323
01:31:01,596 --> 01:31:03,899
But you found one.

1324
01:31:04,933 --> 01:31:06,635
And I know how to exploit it.

1325
01:31:06,768 --> 01:31:09,438
Well, get to the part
where I start to give a shit.

1326
01:31:12,708 --> 01:31:15,143
These are
Eastern Siberian rosary peas.

1327
01:31:15,277 --> 01:31:17,746
A rare species.

1328
01:31:17,879 --> 01:31:20,983
I found their residue
on a poison in the monastery.

1329
01:31:21,116 --> 01:31:25,020
These peas are only native to
a specific region in Siberia.

1330
01:31:26,822 --> 01:31:28,790
That's where we'll find him.

1331
01:31:29,992 --> 01:31:31,994
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

1332
01:31:39,434 --> 01:31:40,402
[CLICKS]

1333
01:31:43,672 --> 01:31:45,474
[SHORT LAUGH]

1334
01:31:46,641 --> 01:31:48,844
[WHIRRING]

1335
01:31:57,786 --> 01:31:59,154
[DOOR OPENS]

1336
01:31:59,287 --> 01:32:01,189
SERGEI:
Whoa, careful with that.

1337
01:32:01,323 --> 01:32:02,958
[DOOR SLAMS SHUT]

1338
01:32:03,091 --> 01:32:04,960
Actually, I'm pretty good
with one of these things.

1339
01:32:05,093 --> 01:32:07,996
Archery at summer camp.

1340
01:32:10,599 --> 01:32:12,868
Figwort.

1341
01:32:13,001 --> 01:32:15,237
Wood avens.

1342
01:32:15,370 --> 01:32:17,339
Tribulus.

1343
01:32:17,472 --> 01:32:19,174
Mm-hmm.

1344
01:32:19,307 --> 01:32:21,343
Rosary peas?

1345
01:32:21,476 --> 01:32:24,212
You seem to know your stuff.

1346
01:32:24,346 --> 01:32:25,580
They'll kill you.

1347
01:32:25,714 --> 01:32:27,049
Or save you.

1348
01:32:27,182 --> 01:32:30,018
Nature's funny like that.

1349
01:32:30,152 --> 01:32:32,220
What are you trying to do here?

1350
01:32:34,856 --> 01:32:37,392
Tell me about this.

1351
01:32:38,427 --> 01:32:40,929
It was my grandmother's.

1352
01:32:41,063 --> 01:32:43,465
We were on safari
visiting her that day.

1353
01:32:43,598 --> 01:32:47,469
I've been trying to figure out
what was in here for years.

1354
01:32:47,602 --> 01:32:52,774
My grandmother was
kind of a... mystic.

1355
01:32:52,908 --> 01:32:55,477
She had a lot of
crazy stuff around.

1356
01:32:55,610 --> 01:32:57,579
My parents didn't like
to talk about it,

1357
01:32:57,712 --> 01:33:00,949
but she was
a very powerful woman.

1358
01:33:02,217 --> 01:33:04,052
She said it would heal
whoever drank it,

1359
01:33:04,186 --> 01:33:08,123
in undreamed-of ways.

1360
01:33:08,256 --> 01:33:10,625
I was... I was just a kid.

1361
01:33:10,759 --> 01:33:13,028
I didn't know
what it would actually do.

1362
01:33:13,161 --> 01:33:14,930
This saved my life.

1363
01:33:15,063 --> 01:33:16,364
Did it?

1364
01:33:16,498 --> 01:33:19,201
-Trust me. It changed me.
-Exactly.

1365
01:33:20,235 --> 01:33:22,704
Look at what you became.

1366
01:33:25,240 --> 01:33:28,643
I need to know
what was in here.

1367
01:33:31,079 --> 01:33:32,681
And if you can get any more.

1368
01:33:32,814 --> 01:33:34,483
No.

1369
01:33:36,418 --> 01:33:38,120
She died not long after
that trip,

1370
01:33:38,253 --> 01:33:39,788
and I never saw her again.

1371
01:33:47,462 --> 01:33:49,599
I heard back
from one of my sources.

1372
01:33:49,731 --> 01:33:52,767
The Rhino's on the move.
We should know more very soon.

1373
01:33:52,901 --> 01:33:55,137
I knew you'd be good at this.

1374
01:33:57,939 --> 01:34:02,010
Sergei, we're gonna
get Dmitri back,

1375
01:34:02,144 --> 01:34:04,446
but is all of this
really worth it?

1376
01:34:04,580 --> 01:34:09,151
Calypso, I was made to do this.

1377
01:34:09,284 --> 01:34:11,353
I'm the greatest hunter
on this planet.

1378
01:34:11,486 --> 01:34:13,355
It's undeniable.

1379
01:34:13,488 --> 01:34:16,024
There's nobody I can't track
down, nobody I can't beat.

1380
01:34:16,158 --> 01:34:18,126
There's nobody can
even touch me, so, no.

1381
01:34:18,260 --> 01:34:19,828
Why would I want to stop?

1382
01:34:19,961 --> 01:34:22,364
It's called karma.
She catches up to you.

1383
01:34:23,431 --> 01:34:24,966
Not me.

1384
01:34:25,100 --> 01:34:26,935
I'm faster than she is.

1385
01:34:30,506 --> 01:34:32,707
But Dmitri wasn't.

1386
01:34:42,817 --> 01:34:44,520
Interesting piece.

1387
01:34:44,654 --> 01:34:47,355
It's gonna take more than
a gun to kill Kraven.

1388
01:34:47,489 --> 01:34:49,991
I find this formula
that was developed by MI6

1389
01:34:50,125 --> 01:34:52,194
to be particularly effective.

1390
01:34:52,327 --> 01:34:53,862
May I?

1391
01:34:55,430 --> 01:34:57,933
-[RAJA WHINING]
-[THE FOREIGNER CLEARS THROAT]

1392
01:34:58,066 --> 01:35:00,603
It first brings on
your darkest nightmares,

1393
01:35:00,735 --> 01:35:03,539
then paralysis
of your vital organs,

1394
01:35:03,673 --> 01:35:05,340
before a most violent death.

1395
01:35:05,473 --> 01:35:07,742
[LAUGHING]

1396
01:35:07,876 --> 01:35:09,679
I like your style.

1397
01:35:15,317 --> 01:35:17,986
[PHONE RINGING]

1398
01:35:20,690 --> 01:35:22,390
Only one person
has this number.

1399
01:35:22,525 --> 01:35:23,858
[PHONE BEEPS]

1400
01:35:23,992 --> 01:35:25,860
Dima, where are you?

1401
01:35:25,994 --> 01:35:28,363
Sergei, I'm sorry.
They made me call you.

1402
01:35:28,496 --> 01:35:29,831
SERGEI:
Dmitri.

1403
01:35:29,965 --> 01:35:31,099
ALEKSEI:
Afraid not.

1404
01:35:31,233 --> 01:35:33,268
But now you know he is alive.

1405
01:35:33,401 --> 01:35:34,769
What do you want?

1406
01:35:34,903 --> 01:35:38,373
A life without looking
over my shoulder.

1407
01:35:38,507 --> 01:35:40,408
You have two choices.

1408
01:35:40,543 --> 01:35:43,044
I know you hate your father
as much as I do,

1409
01:35:43,178 --> 01:35:46,815
so you and I,

1410
01:35:46,948 --> 01:35:50,418
and young Dmitri here,
we work together.

1411
01:35:50,553 --> 01:35:51,721
You could be my partners.

1412
01:35:51,853 --> 01:35:54,055
Or I kill you and burn...

1413
01:35:54,189 --> 01:35:55,290
[PHONE BEEPS]

1414
01:35:59,961 --> 01:36:01,631
Okay, then.

1415
01:36:01,763 --> 01:36:04,165
Now we go hunt the hunter.

1416
01:36:19,381 --> 01:36:21,249
[CHAINS RATTLING]

1417
01:36:21,383 --> 01:36:23,385
Spread out.

1418
01:36:23,519 --> 01:36:26,154
Bring me his body...

1419
01:36:26,288 --> 01:36:28,323
or don't come back.

1420
01:36:29,457 --> 01:36:31,126
[WHIRRING]

1421
01:36:47,275 --> 01:36:49,144
Raja.

1422
01:36:49,277 --> 01:36:51,279
[RAJA GROWLING]

1423
01:36:53,014 --> 01:36:54,883
Where is he?

1424
01:36:55,016 --> 01:36:56,451
[BARKING]

1425
01:36:56,585 --> 01:36:57,620
He's already here.

1426
01:36:57,753 --> 01:36:59,354
-[SNARLING]
-[SCREAMING]

1427
01:36:59,487 --> 01:37:01,323
MAN:
Oh, shit! Look out!

1428
01:37:02,857 --> 01:37:04,527
[SNARLING]

1429
01:37:04,660 --> 01:37:06,461
[MAN SCREAMING]

1430
01:37:13,068 --> 01:37:14,869
[PANTING]

1431
01:37:36,491 --> 01:37:37,660
-[SCREAMS]
-[GRUNTING]

1432
01:37:38,661 --> 01:37:40,028
[GASPS]

1433
01:37:42,997 --> 01:37:44,399
[GRUNTING]

1434
01:37:53,576 --> 01:37:55,043
[CRIES OUT]

1435
01:37:56,244 --> 01:37:58,179
-[TRAPS SNAPPING]
-[SCREAMING]

1436
01:38:00,181 --> 01:38:01,883
[SCREAMING]

1437
01:38:04,018 --> 01:38:06,187
[MEN SCREAMING IN AGONY
IN DISTANCE]

1438
01:38:07,690 --> 01:38:09,023
Amateurs.

1439
01:38:09,157 --> 01:38:10,892
So embarrassing for us.

1440
01:38:11,960 --> 01:38:13,094
Do it.

1441
01:38:14,830 --> 01:38:16,732
-[RADIO BEEPS]
-Start the run.

1442
01:38:20,235 --> 01:38:21,570
[GRUNTING VICIOUSLY]

1443
01:38:22,638 --> 01:38:23,905
-[GRUNTS]
-[CRIES OUT]

1444
01:38:26,742 --> 01:38:28,778
Fire in the hole.

1445
01:38:29,678 --> 01:38:31,246
You got to be kidding.

1446
01:38:37,051 --> 01:38:38,052
[GRUNTS]

1447
01:38:42,357 --> 01:38:44,660
[HELICOPTER BLADES WHIRRING]

1448
01:38:48,898 --> 01:38:50,633
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1449
01:38:50,766 --> 01:38:52,601
[BIRDS CAWING]

1450
01:38:53,736 --> 01:38:54,969
-[DART THUMPS]
-[CRIES OUT]

1451
01:38:56,404 --> 01:38:57,939
Whoa.

1452
01:38:58,072 --> 01:38:59,675
[GRUNTING]

1453
01:38:59,809 --> 01:39:01,510
[GROANING]

1454
01:39:05,614 --> 01:39:07,482
[WHIMPERING]

1455
01:39:07,616 --> 01:39:10,952
[YELLING]

1456
01:39:11,085 --> 01:39:13,221
[DISTORTED VOICES SINGING
IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE]

1457
01:39:13,354 --> 01:39:15,791
[SERGEI GASPING IN FEAR]

1458
01:39:17,225 --> 01:39:18,493
[WHIMPERING]

1459
01:39:23,264 --> 01:39:24,934
[YELLING]

1460
01:39:32,273 --> 01:39:33,909
[GRUNTS]

1461
01:39:35,376 --> 01:39:37,780
THE FOREIGNER: [ECHOING]
The hallucinations

1462
01:39:37,913 --> 01:39:40,448
are just the beginning.

1463
01:39:40,583 --> 01:39:43,017
Are you seeing
your worst nightmares?

1464
01:39:45,420 --> 01:39:46,488
[ECHOING]
One.

1465
01:39:47,623 --> 01:39:49,123
[ECHOING]
Two.

1466
01:39:49,257 --> 01:39:50,860
[PANTING]

1467
01:39:50,992 --> 01:39:52,628
-[ECHOING] Three.
-[GASPS]

1468
01:39:52,761 --> 01:39:54,195
[GRUNTING]

1469
01:39:58,266 --> 01:40:01,069
[ECHOING] As the poison makes
its way to your spinal cord,

1470
01:40:01,202 --> 01:40:04,305
you'll begin to lose
all motor functions.

1471
01:40:04,439 --> 01:40:06,140
Then asphyxiation.

1472
01:40:06,274 --> 01:40:08,376
So, you're the legend.

1473
01:40:10,278 --> 01:40:11,479
The myth.

1474
01:40:11,614 --> 01:40:13,716
[GRUNTING]

1475
01:40:13,849 --> 01:40:16,685
But look at you now.
You're just a man.

1476
01:40:17,987 --> 01:40:20,288
[STRAINED GRUNTING]

1477
01:40:22,490 --> 01:40:23,526
[GRUNTS]

1478
01:40:24,593 --> 01:40:26,361
[GROANING]

1479
01:40:41,010 --> 01:40:43,478
[GROANING]

1480
01:40:50,084 --> 01:40:52,086
[GRUNTING]

1481
01:40:53,822 --> 01:40:56,625
You give him hell, Kraven.

1482
01:40:57,927 --> 01:40:59,394
[GRUNTING, GROANING]

1483
01:40:59,528 --> 01:41:01,262
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1484
01:41:07,235 --> 01:41:10,639
[THE FOREIGNER BREATHES DEEPLY]

1485
01:41:10,773 --> 01:41:13,274
Honestly, I thought
that would be harder.

1486
01:41:13,408 --> 01:41:15,243
[STRAINING]

1487
01:41:15,376 --> 01:41:16,946
[FOOTSTEPS APPROACHING]

1488
01:41:17,078 --> 01:41:18,346
It's done.

1489
01:41:18,479 --> 01:41:20,583
But the brother's
still out there.

1490
01:41:20,716 --> 01:41:22,017
Go find him.

1491
01:41:22,150 --> 01:41:23,284
Let's go.

1492
01:41:24,887 --> 01:41:27,056
-[GROANING]
-[ECHOING] One.

1493
01:41:28,089 --> 01:41:29,257
[ECHOING]
Two.

1494
01:41:29,390 --> 01:41:31,594
-[GRUNTS]
-[GUNSHOT ECHOING]

1495
01:41:31,727 --> 01:41:33,762
Three, motherfucker.

1496
01:41:33,896 --> 01:41:36,130
Goodbye, Kraven the Hunter.

1497
01:41:41,070 --> 01:41:42,705
DMITRI:
Sergei.

1498
01:41:47,108 --> 01:41:49,578
BERT: Can't catch a break,
can you, mate?

1499
01:42:13,836 --> 01:42:16,170
Legends don't die.

1500
01:42:16,304 --> 01:42:18,707
Now get the fuck up, Kraven.

1501
01:42:22,044 --> 01:42:24,013
[WHOOSHING]

1502
01:42:26,715 --> 01:42:28,617
-Up!
-[GASPING]

1503
01:42:28,751 --> 01:42:30,619
[GROANING, COUGHING]

1504
01:42:34,957 --> 01:42:37,026
I knew you had more of that.

1505
01:42:37,158 --> 01:42:39,962
Well, forgive me
for not trusting a lunatic

1506
01:42:40,095 --> 01:42:42,798
with my family's
deepest legacy.

1507
01:42:44,465 --> 01:42:45,834
Get up.

1508
01:42:45,968 --> 01:42:47,268
[STRAINING]
Okay.

1509
01:42:47,402 --> 01:42:49,270
[GROANING]

1510
01:42:50,338 --> 01:42:52,908
Well, that must be
some summer camp.

1511
01:42:53,042 --> 01:42:56,177
You're not the only one
with secrets.

1512
01:42:56,310 --> 01:42:59,014
Don't make me regret this.

1513
01:43:07,656 --> 01:43:09,992
BERT:
It's over.

1514
01:43:10,125 --> 01:43:11,827
Kraven's dead.

1515
01:43:14,228 --> 01:43:15,831
[LAUGHING SOFTLY]

1516
01:43:18,499 --> 01:43:19,935
What a day.

1517
01:43:20,069 --> 01:43:22,071
[LAUGHING]

1518
01:43:26,542 --> 01:43:28,977
Put him in the car.

1519
01:43:29,111 --> 01:43:31,046
Who knows?
Maybe Nikolai will pay,

1520
01:43:31,180 --> 01:43:33,314
now that he has
only one son left.

1521
01:43:50,032 --> 01:43:51,499
[RADIO BEEPS]

1522
01:43:52,868 --> 01:43:57,573
Does anyone else see
what I'm seeing here?

1523
01:44:02,177 --> 01:44:03,912
[GRUNTS]

1524
01:44:04,046 --> 01:44:06,247
[BELLOWING]

1525
01:44:06,380 --> 01:44:07,983
[HUFFING]

1526
01:44:09,718 --> 01:44:10,819
[ALEKSEI SIGHS]

1527
01:44:10,953 --> 01:44:13,055
[HISSING]

1528
01:44:13,956 --> 01:44:15,289
[STRAINED GROANING]

1529
01:44:15,423 --> 01:44:17,458
[GRUNTING]

1530
01:44:17,593 --> 01:44:19,161
[SKIN CRACKLING]

1531
01:44:24,099 --> 01:44:25,200
[SNORTING]

1532
01:44:29,370 --> 01:44:30,371
[BODYGUARDS YELLING]

1533
01:44:30,506 --> 01:44:31,940
[BELLOWING]

1534
01:44:33,374 --> 01:44:35,476
[SCREAMING]

1535
01:44:35,611 --> 01:44:37,478
-[BODYGUARD SCREAMS]
-[BELLOWS]

1536
01:44:37,613 --> 01:44:39,047
[GRUNTING]

1537
01:44:43,519 --> 01:44:44,753
[GRUNTING]

1538
01:44:47,022 --> 01:44:48,957
[YELLING]

1539
01:44:49,091 --> 01:44:51,260
[GRUNTING FIERCELY]

1540
01:44:58,066 --> 01:44:59,868
[DEEP VOICE]
Kraven!

1541
01:45:06,909 --> 01:45:08,277
-[ALEKSEI YELLING]
-[GRUNTS]

1542
01:45:08,977 --> 01:45:10,712
[ALEKSEI GROWLING]

1543
01:45:10,846 --> 01:45:12,114
Gosh, you're really heavy.

1544
01:45:12,247 --> 01:45:13,215
[ROARS]

1545
01:45:16,450 --> 01:45:18,020
[GROWLING]

1546
01:45:22,858 --> 01:45:25,527
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1547
01:45:25,661 --> 01:45:27,596
[YELLING]

1548
01:45:39,575 --> 01:45:41,543
-[SCREAMING]
-[BELLOWING]

1549
01:45:52,020 --> 01:45:53,121
[GRUNTS]

1550
01:45:53,255 --> 01:45:55,123
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1551
01:45:55,257 --> 01:45:57,159
Sergei.

1552
01:45:57,292 --> 01:45:58,660
[METALLIC CREAKING]

1553
01:45:58,794 --> 01:46:01,230
[STRAINED GRUNTING]

1554
01:46:02,865 --> 01:46:04,733
[ALEKSEI YELLING]

1555
01:46:05,734 --> 01:46:07,236
[GRUNTING]

1556
01:46:09,238 --> 01:46:11,240
[GRUNTS]

1557
01:46:11,372 --> 01:46:13,175
[GROWLS]

1558
01:46:15,978 --> 01:46:18,013
[GROANING]

1559
01:46:18,146 --> 01:46:19,781
[BREATHING HEAVILY]

1560
01:46:30,192 --> 01:46:32,426
[GROANING]

1561
01:46:34,162 --> 01:46:35,230
[PAINED GROANING]

1562
01:46:43,739 --> 01:46:45,674
[YELLING]

1563
01:46:46,808 --> 01:46:49,378
[YELLING, GRUNTS]

1564
01:46:50,846 --> 01:46:52,014
[GROWLING]

1565
01:46:55,384 --> 01:46:56,518
[YELLING]

1566
01:46:56,652 --> 01:47:00,055
[CHOKING]

1567
01:47:00,188 --> 01:47:03,491
[STRAINING] My father was
right about one thing.

1568
01:47:03,625 --> 01:47:05,394
You are nothing.

1569
01:47:06,795 --> 01:47:08,263
[SKIN CRACKLING]

1570
01:47:08,397 --> 01:47:09,831
[LOW GROWLING]

1571
01:47:14,269 --> 01:47:15,971
[CRIES OUT]

1572
01:47:16,104 --> 01:47:18,507
[GROANING]

1573
01:47:21,743 --> 01:47:24,413
-[ROARS]
-[GRUNTS]

1574
01:47:30,419 --> 01:47:32,921
[BOTH YELLING]

1575
01:47:38,126 --> 01:47:39,261
[YELLING]

1576
01:47:47,135 --> 01:47:48,236
[SCREAMING]

1577
01:47:55,377 --> 01:47:56,678
[BELLOWING FADES]

1578
01:47:56,812 --> 01:47:59,014
[STRAINED GRUNTING]

1579
01:48:03,685 --> 01:48:05,988
[GURGLING, COUGHING]

1580
01:48:08,924 --> 01:48:11,193
The video of me,
how did you get it?

1581
01:48:11,326 --> 01:48:13,862
[COUGHING, GAGGING]

1582
01:48:13,996 --> 01:48:16,098
Who sent it?

1583
01:48:16,231 --> 01:48:20,736
[STRAINING] How is it
that even the great hunter

1584
01:48:20,869 --> 01:48:27,042
can't see what was always
right in front of him?

1585
01:48:29,478 --> 01:48:30,912
[ALEKSEI COUGHS]

1586
01:48:31,046 --> 01:48:32,147
[GUN RACKS]

1587
01:48:38,120 --> 01:48:40,155
No.

1588
01:48:41,189 --> 01:48:42,991
He deserves to die.

1589
01:48:43,125 --> 01:48:44,292
And he will.

1590
01:48:45,360 --> 01:48:47,129
But, Dmitri, that's not you.

1591
01:48:56,705 --> 01:48:59,041
[STRAINED GURGLING]

1592
01:49:01,276 --> 01:49:02,878
I wish...

1593
01:49:04,514 --> 01:49:07,382
I wish I never met

1594
01:49:07,517 --> 01:49:10,218
you Kravinoffs.

1595
01:49:10,352 --> 01:49:12,554
[GASPING BREATH]

1596
01:49:12,687 --> 01:49:14,723
[EXHALES]

1597
01:49:27,335 --> 01:49:28,870
[WIND HOWLING]

1598
01:49:29,004 --> 01:49:31,206
[RUSTLING, TWIG SNAPPING]

1599
01:49:35,343 --> 01:49:36,611
[SNIFFS]

1600
01:49:39,147 --> 01:49:40,715
[ZIPPER WHIZZING]

1601
01:49:49,091 --> 01:49:50,926
Sergei.

1602
01:49:51,059 --> 01:49:52,894
How did you find me?

1603
01:49:53,929 --> 01:49:55,630
I'm a hunter.

1604
01:49:57,065 --> 01:50:00,202
It's what we do.

1605
01:50:03,539 --> 01:50:08,910
You sent the video
and told The Rhino who I was.

1606
01:50:10,645 --> 01:50:13,915
Did you really think
father would not recognize

1607
01:50:14,049 --> 01:50:15,951
actions of his own son?

1608
01:50:16,084 --> 01:50:19,421
An assassin who uses
all the methods

1609
01:50:19,555 --> 01:50:23,158
of animals of the jungle?

1610
01:50:23,291 --> 01:50:27,597
You, of all people,
should recognize and appreciate

1611
01:50:27,729 --> 01:50:29,731
the beauty of the trap I set.

1612
01:50:29,865 --> 01:50:31,466
[SCOFFS]

1613
01:50:34,069 --> 01:50:37,038
The Rhino was coming for you.

1614
01:50:37,172 --> 01:50:40,108
You weren't strong enough to
fight him off by yourself, huh?

1615
01:50:40,242 --> 01:50:42,344
Exactly.

1616
01:50:42,477 --> 01:50:47,149
But my son,
my real son, Kraven...

1617
01:50:47,282 --> 01:50:48,850
[LAUGHS SOFTLY]

1618
01:50:48,984 --> 01:50:51,019
...no one is stronger.

1619
01:50:52,220 --> 01:50:57,425
And I knew you would not
go after him for me.

1620
01:50:59,494 --> 01:51:01,631
So, I sent him after you.

1621
01:51:02,632 --> 01:51:04,600
Some trap.

1622
01:51:06,001 --> 01:51:06,968
[EXHALES]

1623
01:51:07,102 --> 01:51:08,604
I mean, Dmitri could have died,

1624
01:51:08,737 --> 01:51:10,805
but that's the price
of doing business, right?

1625
01:51:10,939 --> 01:51:12,474
No, no, no, no, no.

1626
01:51:12,608 --> 01:51:16,478
Because I know you would not
let anything happen

1627
01:51:16,612 --> 01:51:18,581
to our precious Dmitri.

1628
01:51:18,713 --> 01:51:19,915
SERGEI:
Hmm.

1629
01:51:20,048 --> 01:51:22,484
Our empire is secure.

1630
01:51:22,618 --> 01:51:24,052
So, what now?

1631
01:51:24,186 --> 01:51:25,754
Papa, do we...

1632
01:51:27,523 --> 01:51:29,424
...forget about the past?

1633
01:51:29,559 --> 01:51:32,662
Imagine a future together?

1634
01:51:34,196 --> 01:51:35,697
As family.

1635
01:51:40,035 --> 01:51:41,303
[SIGHS]

1636
01:51:49,477 --> 01:51:51,313
Sergei.

1637
01:51:51,446 --> 01:51:53,549
Where are you going?

1638
01:51:59,454 --> 01:52:02,424
I could have come for you,

1639
01:52:02,558 --> 01:52:05,193
years ago,

1640
01:52:05,327 --> 01:52:07,028
but I didn't.

1641
01:52:08,296 --> 01:52:10,700
After everything you'd done,

1642
01:52:10,832 --> 01:52:13,034
all the pain
you put in the world...

1643
01:52:15,403 --> 01:52:17,573
...you were my father.

1644
01:52:19,107 --> 01:52:20,809
I still am.

1645
01:52:22,043 --> 01:52:23,311
Sit.

1646
01:52:36,791 --> 01:52:38,460
"Never fear death."

1647
01:52:39,894 --> 01:52:42,097
Isn't that what you taught me?

1648
01:52:47,435 --> 01:52:48,937
[BRANCHES CRACKING]

1649
01:52:49,070 --> 01:52:50,939
[DISTANT BELLOWING]

1650
01:52:54,009 --> 01:52:56,612
[BELLOWING CONTINUES]

1651
01:53:01,349 --> 01:53:03,118
[BELLOWING CONTINUES]

1652
01:53:03,251 --> 01:53:05,086
[SNARLING ROAR]

1653
01:53:05,220 --> 01:53:06,788
[NIKOLAI SCREAMING]

1654
01:53:06,921 --> 01:53:08,823
[ROARING CONTINUES]

1655
01:53:16,865 --> 01:53:19,834
[PIANO PLAYING "CHANGES"
BY BLACK SABBATH]

1656
01:53:25,106 --> 01:53:28,611
DMITRI: [IMPERSONATING OZZY
OSBOURNE] <i>♪ I feel unhappy ♪</i>

1657
01:53:30,078 --> 01:53:32,715
<i>♪ I feel so sad ♪</i>

1658
01:53:34,416 --> 01:53:37,152
<i>♪ I've lost the best friend ♪</i>

1659
01:53:38,420 --> 01:53:41,657
<i>♪ That I ever had ♪</i>

1660
01:53:45,594 --> 01:53:52,601
<i>♪ I'm going through changes ♪</i>

1661
01:53:57,939 --> 01:54:00,375
-[SCATTERED APPLAUSE]
-SERGEI: Happy Birthday, Dima.

1662
01:54:01,443 --> 01:54:02,712
It is a happy birthday.

1663
01:54:04,346 --> 01:54:05,681
First one in a long time.

1664
01:54:06,816 --> 01:54:08,517
And that's thanks
to you, Sergei.

1665
01:54:08,651 --> 01:54:10,151
Ah, come on.

1666
01:54:10,285 --> 01:54:12,053
-Or Kraven, should I say.
-Nah.

1667
01:54:12,187 --> 01:54:14,222
What do I call you now?
Mr. Kraven?

1668
01:54:14,356 --> 01:54:16,991
-You know who I am.
-I know you.

1669
01:54:19,894 --> 01:54:22,897
That was, um... hell,

1670
01:54:23,031 --> 01:54:24,567
what I went through.

1671
01:54:24,700 --> 01:54:27,402
But it also freed me.

1672
01:54:27,536 --> 01:54:32,240
U-Um, I feel almost born again.

1673
01:54:32,374 --> 01:54:33,843
[SHORT LAUGH]

1674
01:54:33,975 --> 01:54:36,679
I found a doctor in New York.

1675
01:54:36,812 --> 01:54:39,381
A little unorthodox,
I must admit.

1676
01:54:39,515 --> 01:54:41,517
Mm-hmm.

1677
01:54:41,650 --> 01:54:44,018
But he really helped me.

1678
01:54:44,152 --> 01:54:46,421
I mean...

1679
01:54:46,555 --> 01:54:48,022
changed me.

1680
01:54:48,156 --> 01:54:49,759
How so?

1681
01:54:49,891 --> 01:54:51,594
Hang on a sec.

1682
01:54:51,727 --> 01:54:53,161
Huh?

1683
01:54:54,195 --> 01:54:55,865
-[WHISPERING]
-Mm-hmm.

1684
01:54:57,399 --> 01:54:59,869
[SPEAKING RUSSIAN]

1685
01:55:00,001 --> 01:55:02,370
Since when did you have friends
in the bratva, huh?

1686
01:55:02,505 --> 01:55:03,706
Well, I have business

1687
01:55:03,839 --> 01:55:05,440
-with lots of people.
-Business?

1688
01:55:05,574 --> 01:55:07,610
I thought you said you were
gonna sell Papa's assets

1689
01:55:07,743 --> 01:55:09,344
and get out of the business.

1690
01:55:09,477 --> 01:55:11,413
-I changed my mind.
-Dima, I didn't pull your ass

1691
01:55:11,547 --> 01:55:14,182
out of the fire so you can
become a man like our father.

1692
01:55:14,315 --> 01:55:15,250
Are you serious?

1693
01:55:15,383 --> 01:55:17,218
You put my ass in that fire.

1694
01:55:17,352 --> 01:55:18,920
You're a man
just like our father.

1695
01:55:19,053 --> 01:55:21,724
No, I'm nothing like him.
I have a code.

1696
01:55:21,857 --> 01:55:24,492
-And you're different than him?
-I'm better than him.

1697
01:55:24,627 --> 01:55:26,829
You're... [CHUCKLES]
You're not better than him.

1698
01:55:26,961 --> 01:55:27,962
You're worse.

1699
01:55:28,963 --> 01:55:30,766
How did Papa die again?

1700
01:55:30,900 --> 01:55:32,635
[SERGEI BREATHES DEEPLY]

1701
01:55:32,768 --> 01:55:35,771
A hunting accident, was it?

1702
01:55:35,905 --> 01:55:38,674
Don't lie to me.

1703
01:55:38,808 --> 01:55:41,811
You think you have
some kind of honor, huh?

1704
01:55:41,943 --> 01:55:43,411
Some kind of code?

1705
01:55:44,446 --> 01:55:46,749
Bullshit.

1706
01:55:46,882 --> 01:55:52,320
You're just another man
hunting for a trophy.

1707
01:56:01,362 --> 01:56:02,932
SERGEI:
Hey.

1708
01:56:05,534 --> 01:56:06,936
Dmitri.

1709
01:56:13,107 --> 01:56:14,810
[SCOFFS]

1710
01:56:14,944 --> 01:56:18,079
[SERGEI'S VOICE] You should
see the look on your face.

1711
01:56:26,421 --> 01:56:27,957
Hey.

1712
01:56:31,861 --> 01:56:33,361
Dmitri.

1713
01:56:33,495 --> 01:56:35,396
DMITRI: [NORMAL VOICE]
You know me.

1714
01:56:35,531 --> 01:56:37,065
I've always been a chameleon.

1715
01:56:38,934 --> 01:56:41,236
It's the one thing
I was ever good at.

1716
01:56:41,369 --> 01:56:44,472
Who is this doctor?
What did he do to you?

1717
01:56:44,607 --> 01:56:47,977
You want me to be weak,
so that you can be strong.

1718
01:56:48,109 --> 01:56:49,879
But I'm strong now.

1719
01:56:51,012 --> 01:56:52,648
I can be whoever I want to be.

1720
01:56:52,781 --> 01:56:55,450
The Rhino is gone. Dad is gone.

1721
01:56:55,584 --> 01:56:58,988
It's all just there,
for the taking.

1722
01:57:00,823 --> 01:57:02,892
I'm gonna take it.

1723
01:57:07,161 --> 01:57:09,397
You know I can't
let you do that.

1724
01:57:13,167 --> 01:57:15,538
Go home, Kraven.

1725
01:57:20,509 --> 01:57:22,511
Dad left you something.

1726
01:57:22,645 --> 01:57:24,613
[DISTANT SIREN WAILING]

1727
01:57:28,416 --> 01:57:30,418
[VOICES SINGING
TRADITIONAL MUSIC FAINTLY]

1728
01:57:56,311 --> 01:57:58,079
NIKOLAI: [VOICE-OVER]
<i>"Sergei,</i>

1729
01:57:58,212 --> 01:58:00,516
<i>"each of us has path to walk.</i>

1730
01:58:01,584 --> 01:58:04,185
<i>"Embrace who you really are,</i>

1731
01:58:04,319 --> 01:58:06,689
<i>"and you will have the strength</i>
<i>to walk it.</i>

1732
01:58:08,089 --> 01:58:10,559
<i>"You are more than my child.</i>

1733
01:58:12,027 --> 01:58:14,029
<i>"You are me.</i>

1734
01:58:15,263 --> 01:58:17,733
<i>"And I am you.</i>

1735
01:58:22,771 --> 01:58:24,607
<i>"We are hunters.</i>

1736
01:58:26,909 --> 01:58:29,778
<i>The greatest</i>
<i>the world has ever known."</i>

1737
01:58:31,547 --> 01:58:33,515
[VOICES CONTINUE SINGING
TRADITIONAL MUSIC]

1738
02:00:29,698 --> 02:00:31,700
[SINGING ENDS]

1739
02:06:49,044 --> 02:06:51,012
[MUSIC ENDS]